Kampong Pranak Market in Preah Vihear City Will Open Tomorrow, Commission and Traders Thank Samdech Techo Hun Sen for Providing Funds to Develop the Market
(Preah Vihear): Kampong Pranak Market, located in Kandal Village, Sangkat Kampong Pranak, Preah Vihear City, Preah Vihear Province, will reopen for traders on the morning of September 10, 2021, after being temporarily closed for some time. To prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
After the Kampong Pranak market was temporarily closed to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Preah Vihear provincial governor Prak Sovann requested funding from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to develop the market. Aesthetics again. Among them, 3 concrete roads around the market were developed, a total of 620 meters, 10 meters wide, and 1,240 meters of drainage was installed on both sides of the road.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovann and Ms. Sar Cheng also donated another 42 million Riels to participate in the development of Kampong Pranak Market. Of that, 8 million riels for organizing the media by buying a set of microphones and amplifiers to equip the market.
Another 5 million riels to buy solar lights around the market and improve the aesthetics of the market and another 29 million riels to support food for officials and law enforcement, as well as to pay for machinery.
The Market Committee and Kampong Pranak Market Businessmen would like to express their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as Mr. Prak Sovann and many other philanthropists. Donate money for the development of Kampong Pranak market.
