Afghanistan: Protesters finally cancel protests after Taliban authorities warn of harsh legal action
(Kabul): Protest organizers in Kabul decided to cancel their rally on Thursday after Taliban authorities banned all protests and warned of "severe legal action" against those responsible. Dare to offend. This was released by Reuters on Thursday evening, September 9, 2021.
News reports from Kabul said earlier this week that Taliban armed forces had fired rockets into the air to threaten protesters to disperse in Kabul. Separately, for the cities of Faizabad in the northeast and Herat in the west, two people were shot dead during the protests.
On Wednesday, Taliban authorities warned that protests could not be waived. Taliban authorities say protests must be approved by the Ministry of Justice, and for now no demonstrations are allowed.
The past protests have been the most targeted against Pakistan. Pakistan has been accused by the Afghan protesters of being the biggest supporter and supporter of the Taliban, which has raised concerns among Afghans that the Taliban could be under its influence. Or follow the orders of Islamabad without independence.
