The following is a statement from the Ministry of Tourism: The Suez Canal was blocked again after a container ship capsized on Thursday.
(Cairo): According to local media reports, the Suez Canal Authority has decided to close the canal traffic after a container ship was stranded on Thursday. This is according to the release by The Nation on Thursday night, September 9, 2021.
Authorities told the media that the ship was stranded at a distance of 54 kilometers from the world's major canals.
Four ships from the port of Said en route to the Suez Canal were barred from crossing as authorities quickly mobilized rescue teams to try to retrieve the ship, the report said.
