Greater Mekong Subregion approves strategic framework for 2030
The 7th GMS Summit was videotaped on the morning of September 9, 2021 under the theme "Greater Mekong Subregion: Strengthening to Meet the Challenges of the New Decade" with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presides.
"Recognizing that the new decade has brought new trends, growing threats, as well as new opportunities, we fully support the need for a new roadmap for the future," the statement said. "Therefore, we approve the Greater Mekong Subregion Strategic Framework 2030 or GMS 2030."
The Greater Mekong Subregion also supports the focus of GMS 2030 to seize opportunities in an interconnected global economy and promote an open, fair and non-discriminatory business environment supported by digital and innovative economies. Greater Mekong Subregion will strengthen digital infrastructure, accelerate digital transformation, promote the use of technology and narrow the digital gap.
Recognizing the need for effective implementation of GMS 2030, the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) provides mandates to Ministers and Senior Officials to develop practical and viable projects to support GMS 2030 operational priorities and strategic frameworks and programs. A GMS that will promote and direct dialogue, policies and specific actions towards achieving the Greater Mekong Subregion vision.
At the same time, the Greater Mekong Subregion wishes to promote regional cooperation and integration, as well as to facilitate trade and investment liberalization and investment. At the same time, the GMS encourages GMS member states to speed up domestic ratification procedures to facilitate the entry into force of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement in the region as soon as possible.
The Greater Mekong Subregion is also committed to taking concrete steps to further strengthen the GMS Economic Corridor Forum and the GMS Governors' Forum and to maintain its annual hosting of both forums.
