China pledges $ 31 million in emergency aid to Afghanistan
BEIJING: China has pledged $ 31 million in aid to Afghanistan, including food supplies and the COVID-19 vaccine. This is according to the release by the BBC on Thursday, September 9, 2021.
The pledge comes as Beijing says it is ready to maintain ties with the Taliban government and that the formation of a new interim government is "a necessary step to restore order" in Afghanistan. .
Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi announced measures to provide aid to Afghanistan at a meeting on Wednesday with the participation of counterparts from neighboring Afghanistan, Pakistan, Iran, Tajikistan, Uzbekistan and Afghanistan. Turkmenistan as well.
At the meeting, Wang Yi also called on these countries to cooperate in helping Afghanistan, adding that China would also provide 3 million doses of vaccine aid to the country.
Taliban officials consider China as Afghanistan's most important partner and have hoped for Chinese investment and support to rebuild the country, which has been torn apart by 20 years of war. Cambodia plans to launch cashew policy later this year
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia plans to launch a national policy on cashews by the end of 2021 or early 2022, while this policy is currently in the meeting to discuss and provide additional input from the inter-ministerial working group led by Ministry of Commerce.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Reach Ra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Deputy Chairman of the Joint Working Group, confirmed that as of the beginning of September 2021, the process of drafting a national policy on cashews is under review and discussion. Enter to fill out.
He added that the plan is to be implemented after the national policy is approved by the plenary session of the Council of Ministers after the draft is finalized at the inter-ministerial level.
Mr. Reach Ra stated that "Currently, the Joint Working Group is speeding up the adjustment of the collection of additional inputs to be completed at the inter-ministerial level and continue to request the submission and final review in the plenary session of the Council of Ministers for approval at the end. 2021 or early 2022. "
In addition, Mr. Reach Ra said that this policy will benefit by turning Cambodia into a major producer and supplier of cashew products to serve the local, regional and global markets.
He said the policy aims to boost production and productivity, promote industrialization, promote competitive excellence and add value to stakeholders in the value chain to support existing actors.
In particular, farmers, growers and attract more investment, as well as maintaining old markets and finding new markets sustainably, as well as creating jobs and income for local people and increase national economic growth. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Reach Ra.
The Secretary of State also said that the Ministry of Commerce has been cooperating with relevant ministries and institutions to update data on the draft national policy on cashews.
While the cashew products of the world's major producers are not growing, Cambodia's cashew products can gain market share from the United States, Germany, the Netherlands, China, the United Kingdom, France, Australia, Canada, the United Arab Emirates and Japan.
The trend of European demand for cashew nuts is currently increasing on the use of cashew nuts instead of other grains that are scarce and more expensive.
Past studies have shown that the Cambodian cashew processing industry is linked to other relevant sectors in order to revitalize the local economy, which adds value through processing, such as:
Roasted and raw cashew nuts are more popular than other grains because they are delicious and healthy.
The National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 has been formulated and sharpened in line with the vision of the Royal Government, as well as consistent with other relevant policy documents and strategies, especially in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy.
