The above expectations were expressed during a bilateral meeting between Mr. Chung Yae-young, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, held on the morning of September 08, 2021. Opportunity for the official visit of the head of the Cambodian diplomatic mission to this country.
"The two Ministers are also optimistic that the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Free Trade Agreement (CKFTA), which will be signed in early October, will help boost bilateral trade and investment," the Foreign Ministry said. "In addition, it will help accelerate the economic recovery of the two countries after the Kovid-19 crisis."
The two ministers were also pleased, noting the stability of bilateral trade between the two countries and the growth of Republic of Korea investment in Cambodia, despite the spread of Kovid-19.
Following the announcement of the formal conclusion of negotiations on the free trade agreement, the two countries will implement domestic procedures for the signing of the bilateral agreement, which is scheduled to take place in mid-2021.
Negotiations on the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement aim to strengthen economic partnership and expand bilateral trade liberalization, mutually beneficial, aimed at enhancing economic benefits and the well-being of people and business. Of both countries.
The Republic of Korea can also help boost its exports to Cambodia, including vehicles, electronics, electronics, beverages, pharmaceuticals and plastic products.
