South Korea commends Cambodian government for timely vaccination campaign nationwide
(Phnom Penh): The South Korean government has commended the Royal Government of Cambodia for launching effective measures to combat Kovid-19 along with timely vaccination campaigns across the country. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia on September 9, 2021.
The South Korean government paid a courtesy call on Foreign Minister of the Republic of Korea Chung Ye-young and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, at a bilateral meeting on the morning of August 8. September 2021 on the occasion of the visit of the head of the Cambodian diplomatic mission to this country.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "The Foreign Minister of the Republic of Korea commends the Royal Government of Cambodia for its effective measures to combat Kovid-19 and its timely vaccination campaign throughout the country. Country. He also praised Cambodia for providing generous assistance to neighboring countries to help them fight Kovid-19.
Deputy Prime Ministers Prak Sokhon and Chung Yeong noted with great satisfaction the continued development of bilateral relations and cooperation in all fields between the two countries in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks. High-level exchanges of frequent visits between the two countries.
As Cambodia and the Republic of Korea mark the 25th anniversary of the re-establishment of diplomatic ties next year, the two Foreign Ministers reaffirmed their commitment to strengthening and expanding the existing bilateral relations. More for the common good of both nations and for peace, security, stability and prosperity in the region and the world.
In this regard, the two Ministers discussed ways and means to deepen cooperation in the fields of military, trade, investment, agriculture, employment, health, communication and information technology, science and innovation, tourism, education and the environment.
The two ministers are also optimistic that the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Free Trade Agreement (CKFTA), to be signed in early October, will further boost bilateral trade and investment and accelerate economic recovery. Of the two countries again after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon thanked the Government of the Republic of Korea for providing development assistance to Cambodia, which has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development.
He stressed that Cambodia appreciates the Republic of Korea's efforts to expand development assistance under the New South Policy and welcomes the New South Policy, which focuses on seven key areas. That includes comprehensive cooperation in the fields of health and medicine.
The Deputy Prime Minister commended the Government and people of Korea for their effective control of the spread of Kovid-19, which has accelerated socio-economic recovery, and praised the Republic of Korea's active role in the framework. Multilateral Vaccination District. He also expressed Cambodia's gratitude to the Government of the Republic of Korea for donating and supplying medical equipment to Cambodia to fight Kovid-19.
The Deputy Prime Minister expressed his sincere gratitude to the Korean Government for taking great care of the Cambodian community in Korea.
In response, Chung Yeong thanked the Cambodian community in Korea for its positive contribution to economic development and cultural diversity in Korea. The Republic of Korea has promised to increase the number of Cambodian workers' quotas and the number of scholarships to Cambodia in the future.
Chung Yeong reiterated that as Cambodia is one of the priority partners in the official development assistance program and a core partner in the Republic of Korea's new South Korea policy, the Republic of Korea will continue to assist and cooperate with Cambodia in the areas of water management, public health, transportation, education and other essential sectors in Cambodia.
The Foreign Minister of the Republic of Korea praised Cambodia's active role in peacekeeping operations under the United Nations umbrella in Africa and the Middle East, which has contributed to peace and stability in those areas, and thanked Cambodia for Active role in facilitating relations within the framework of the ASEAN-ROK Dialogue Partnership and Mekong-Republic of Korea Cooperation.
In addressing the challenges of climate change, the Deputy Prime Minister congratulated the Republic of Korea on its success in hosting the Second Summit on Partnership for Green Development and Global Goals 2030 in May. We strongly support the new green policy and commitment of the Korean government on carbon neutrality by 2050.
The Foreign Minister of the Republic of Korea expressed his appreciation to Prime Minister Hun Sen for his contribution to the success of the summit, while also emphasizing the need for green technology development.
