BEIJING: On the eve of the 20th anniversary of the September 11 terrorist attacks, the US-inspired war in Afghanistan ended in failure. In the last phase of the evacuation of US troops, the extremist group ISIS carried out a series of bombings in the Afghan capital, Kabul, killing more than 100 people, including 13 US soldiers. Well.
What they call the "war on terror" that lasted for 20 years cost more than $ 2 trillion and left more than 20,000 American soldiers dead and wounded. Why did it end in failure? Seriously like this? This makes the whole world think of mistakes.
As some analysts have suggested, one of the main reasons is that in the case of counter-terrorism, the US has focused on its own interests and has applied different standards when judging terrorism and acts of terrorism. Thus, duplicate standards in counter-terrorism issues have allowed the spread of terrorism.
In fact, when the United States first sent troops to Afghanistan and Iraq, the United States also tried to link counterterrorism to the practice of hegemony and subversion of other countries. Thus, the so-called "counter-terrorism", which includes personal intentions, has in fact exacerbated the conflict and unrest in the region and the countries involved, leading to a series of terrorist attacks.
