BEIJING: From September 2013 to the present, the "Belt and Road" initiative proposed by Chinese President Xi Jinping has been running for eight years. Over the past eight years, the initiative has evolved from a day-to-day maturity with a wide range of scope and influence, becoming a new artery of the global economy.
We look back at the "Belt and Road", an acronym for the "Silk Road Economic Belt" and the "21st Century Maritime Silk Road" today, which is much broader and more widely recognized. And the participation of many partner countries and regions to share the achievements of joint construction, joint development in the sense of achieving common prosperity, which is the desire of people all over the world.
As of the end of January 2021, 140 countries and 31 international organizations have signed 205 cooperation documents on the joint construction of the "Belt and Road" with China, which demonstrate the "Belt" initiative. And Roads ”has become the largest international cooperation forum in the world.
Especially after the two countries, Cambodia and China, assumed to be "steel friends", cooperation in all fields has become closer, while the "Belt and Road" initiative has acted as a cohesive driving force. With Cambodia's "Rectangular Strategy". Given the growing volume of bilateral trade, it is not difficult to see that the two countries are naturally favorable partners.
In addition to Cambodia, which has benefited from a series of "Belt and Road" initiatives, other partner countries around the world have also benefited from the joint construction of the "Belt and Road". In particular, developing countries that have linked their national policies or strategies with this initiative have all achieved achievements in many areas to develop the nation as well as improve the living standards of the people.
