Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Solidarity cooperation under multilateral mechanism is the key to building the Greater Mekong Subregion from the Kovid 19 crisis
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, sees that accelerating the implementation of cooperation programs and promoting solidarity under a multilateral mechanism is the key to ensuring a successful recovery. Strong social and economic development for the Greater Mekong Subregion after the end of the Kovid 19 crisis.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that the meeting held under the above theme aims to reflect our strong joint commitment to jointly pave the way for solving new challenges. The success will ensure that the Greater Mekong Subregion will remain at the heart of regional connectivity and help member countries achieve their goals of sustainable and inclusive development.
While highlighting the progress and achievements of the Greater Mekong Subregion through the cooperation of the past six years, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the challenges for the Greater Mekong Subregion. Well. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Kovid 19 outbreak is a new obstacle and challenge for the development of the Greater Mekong Subregion.
"Currently, although we expect the WV 19 crisis to ease in the near future due to the momentum and expansion of vaccination in each country is progressing well, the whole world is still facing," he said. "And the risk of a new wave of disease caused by a new mutant virus that will continue to disrupt social and economic activities, from public health to tourism to disruption of the global supply chain."
In order to revive the economy of the Greater Mekong Subregion after the end of the Kovid 19 crisis, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has drawn the attention of the GMS member countries to focus on cooperation, the fight against Kovid 19, Mobilize financial resources and connections.
Regarding the fight against Kovid 19, the Prime Minister said that the Mekong countries' efforts to fight Kovid 19 by introducing appropriate interventions to prevent the spread of the disease reduce the impact. Affect the operation of the economy and ensure the stability of people's lives.
In relation to the fight against Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the role of the People's Republic of China in providing vaccines against Kovid 19 to countries in the region. He also thanked the international community for sharing and providing vaccines through the World Health Organization's COVAX program and bilateral assistance to Cambodia.
For Samdech Techo, this is a demonstration of friendship and solidarity in an emergency situation, as Samdech once said, "Love each other in times of need, know good friends in difficult times", which will contribute to the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in The road to normalcy and economic recovery after the Kovid 19 crisis.
At the same time, public-private partnerships are key mechanisms that will help ease financing difficulties.
Regarding regional connectivity, which is at the heart of Greater Mekong Subregion cooperation, Hun Sen stressed the importance of digital connectivity for compensating for productivity lost due to the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as ensuring efficiency and sustainability. Of Socio-Economic Development.
