In this speech, Samdech Techo Hun Sen warmly welcomed the presence of the leaders of the Mekong countries and the President of the Asian Development Bank. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is honored to play a role in facilitating the review and development of a new strategic framework that sets the future direction for the Greater Mekong Subregion Cooperation Program on the path to development towards common prosperity based on the principles International law, peace and unity.
In his opening remarks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the progress, challenges and work directions for the Greater Mekong Subregion.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the challenges of Kovid 19 virus, which affects the development goals for the Greater Mekong Subregion. However, Samdech Techo noted that the Greater Mekong Subregion has made great efforts to combat this global epidemic.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted that China has become a country that plays an important role in the fight against Kovid 19 by sharing a large number of vaccines to countries in the region. Samdech Techo also took the opportunity to thank the Chinese government and partner countries through the Kovak mechanism for providing vaccine assistance to Cambodia.
In his opening remarks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced a number of visions to contribute to the development of the environment for the Greater Mekong Subregion.
