In the first half of this year, the Royal Government of Cambodia did not sign a new loan and loan agreement
"In the first half of 2021, no new concessional loan agreements were signed as the new development programs / projects are in the study and preparation phase "Delayed by the spread of Kovid 19."
According to the Ministry of Economy, from 1993 until the end of the first half of 2021, the Royal Government has signed concessional loan agreements with development partners totaling 14.84 billion US dollars, including: The physical infrastructure sector covers About 84% and other priority sectors about 16%.
In the first half of 2021, the Royal Government withdrew a total of 545.96 million US dollars from the development partners, of which: the bilateral framework was about 78%, equivalent to 426.39 million US dollars and the framework Multilateral accounts accounted for 22% of the $ 119.57 million.
From 1993 until the end of the first half of 2021, the Royal Government withdrew a total of US $ 10.05 billion in cash from development partners, equivalent to approximately 68% of the total concessional loans. About 81% of the above concessional loans were used to finance public investment projects in the physical infrastructure sector and about 19% in other priority sectors.
In the first half of 2021, the Royal Government paid a total of 197.40 million US dollars in debt services to development partners, including 147.05 million US dollars in principal and 50.34 million US dollars in interest and other fees. From 1993 until the end of the first half of 2021, the Royal Government owed a total of $ 2.29 billion in debt service to development partners, including:
