Literacy also contributes to the achievement of the Millennium Development Goals 2016-2030, especially to achieve the goal of the new facility is to turn the labor force into the use of professional skills in accordance with Cambodia's "new growth strategy".
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron added that Cambodia is in a precarious situation due to Kovid 19, so this literacy class and the opportunity for young people to continue their education throughout life must be weighed against age protection. The lives of teachers and students that require us to be creative and contribute to the government to promote the prevention of measles 19 and provide opportunities for young people to continue their education.
The minister said that the 21st century has entered a new phase, digital literacy, which includes traditional literacy, which has already been practiced and requires students to use technology, including education providers. Set up a digital system to respond to new situations that require the use of technology to educate young people.
He added that if only the traditional literacy class, finding a job in this new era is also difficult, so the Ministry has set a goal by turning some community learning centers into lifelong learning centers and integrate Technology for young people to use technology in order to strengthen the opportunity to get a good job for young people, and if not meet the new needs, this national literacy program can not be successful.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Information considers that the Cambodian statement is intended to mislead the public by making baseless allegations against the competent authorities performing their legal duties.
(Phnom Penh): Spokesman of the Ministry of Information, Mr. Meas Sophorn, through Fresh News on September 08, 2021, considered that the statement of the Cambodian Journalists Association (CamboJA) intended to mislead the public. Accusations without a clear and specific basis against the competent authorities performing their legal duties as obstruction, threat, violation of journalists' right to access information.
Regarding this case, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Information stated the following 5 points:
1. These statements are intended to mislead the public by making unfounded and unspecified allegations against the competent authorities who perform their legal duties as obstruction, threat, violation of journalists' right to access information.
2. When the competent authority is conducting a mission or conducting an operation at any location or place, the authority has the right not to allow the person without relevant authority, including journalists, to enter the location or place where the competent authority is conducting the mission or operation because it may Affects or disturbs as an obstacle, obstructs or may endanger the competent authority who is performing its duties and responsibilities in that mission or operation.
3. Journalists have the right to receive information from all sources related to any event or event or operation and to publish accurate and comprehensive information according to the source they receive, but if the journalist does not Look for sources from all parties involved in any incident or event or operation that is a journalist who violates the rights of others.
4. Any person or party who feels that he or she has been violated or threatened by any person or party has the right to file a complaint to the court in accordance with the law to seek or demand justice or justice for himself / herself. Seek justice or justice in the air or on the streets.
5. The issuance of a statement condemning or indicting any person or party should be examined and investigated as clearly and precisely as possible to avoid when the accused person or party exercises legal rights. In order to protect their right or justice, they are accused of using the law to intimidate, threaten or persecute themselves.
