Australian Ambassador to Cambodia warns Cambodians to beware of Australian agricultural visa schemes as Cambodia-Australia does not yet have them
(Phnom Penh): The Australian Embassy in Cambodia has confirmed that there is currently no bilateral agricultural visa between Australia and Cambodia.
At the same time, the Embassy urges Cambodians to be wary of any companies that claim to be able to arrange agricultural visas for Australia today. This is according to a press release from the Australian Embassy in Cambodia on the current Australian Agricultural Visa Program, which Fresh News received on the afternoon of September 8, 2021.
On 23 August 2021, the Australian Government announced the launch of a new Australian Agricultural Visa Program. The embassy will negotiate with bilateral partners on visa arrangements, starting with a number of countries before expanding to more countries in the future.
Details on how to apply and obtain a visa will be made through the application process in consultation with the Australian Department of Agriculture. The Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade administers the visa. The Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Agriculture, Water and Environment will provide operational support to ensure visa integrity as well as to meet the needs of the agricultural and primary industries.
Minimum standards to protect workers from exploitation are important and will be modeled on Australia's successful Pacific Labor mobility program. Once visa arrangements are completed, there will be strict rules to protect workers. The government is committed to ensuring that all workers have the opportunity to make a positive contribution to the Australian economy without fear of exploitation.
