According to the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak and Mr. Gan Kim Yong discussed the importance of strengthening trade and investment relations between Cambodia and Singapore, and the progress of the ratification process on the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement. (RCEP) between ASEAN and its member countries, and in particular Cambodia's readiness to host the ASEAN Chairmanship and to prepare for the upcoming 2022 meetings.
Mr. Pan Sosak also informed the Singaporean side of the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to control and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease. In particular, the vaccination campaign for all Cambodians and foreigners is an important factor for socio-economic recovery.
The Minister also briefed on Cambodia-Singapore trade and investment relations and cooperation that both sides should focus on in socio-economic recovery, including continuing to ensure the flow of goods, matching business, strengthening trade. Electronics Building regional supply chains and increasing Singapore's investment in Cambodia.
