(Kampong Thom): In order to improve the livelihood of the people in reducing poverty and contributing to the government during the Kovid 19 era, on September 7, 2021, the Kampong Thom Local Council Association has donated to poor people. 140 families in Kampong Thom province in the presence of Mr. Kieng Sengky, President of Kampong Thom Local Council Association, with the participation of members of partner organizations, local authorities.
In fact, vulnerable families, widows and the elderly received humanitarian donations from the Kampong Thom Local Council Association to alleviate some of the hardships of the 19 Kovid period, although the donations distributed at this time were small.
Mr. Kieng Sengky instructed people to use food properly, keep proper documents and be careful of thunder and wind, educate children to stay away from drugs while driving, wear helmets and wear seat belts. Avoid traffic accidents and participate in preventing Kovid 19 by following the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
At the same time, the people and local authorities thanked the Kampong Thom Local Council Association, partner organizations and the Royal Government for taking care of the needy people without leaving any people to starve. .
It should be noted that 140 families received, including 30 families in Tang Kork district, 30 families in Baray district, 30 families in Kampong Svay district, 20 families in Santuk district, 20 families in Prasat Sambo district and 10 families in Stung Sen city, with 50 kilograms of rice per family. 1 gram of noodles, 1 bottle of cooking oil, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish, 1 stick of mask, 1 box of mosquito nets, 1 blanket and 4 bars of soap.
