(Kratie): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), told Fresh News on September 7, 2021 that Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has completed the test operation of a 115 kV transmission line. About 100 km from Kampong Cham to Prek Prosop district and Prek Prosop 115/22 kV substation with 50MVA in Prek Prosop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that the new transmission line and substation is part of a cooperation project between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the French Republic through the French Development Agency (ADF), which provides concessional loans to EDC to increase the scope of supply. Quality, stability and sustainability.
This substation can supply more directly to Prek Prosop district, help to Sambo district, Stung Trang district and partly reserve to help Kratie city in case of any inconvenience.
