Flooding in Takhmao City Caused by Blockage of Drainage System, Kandal Provincial Governor Orders Takhmao City Governor and Director of Public Department to Drain Immediately
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, ordered the professional officers of Takhmao City Authority, especially the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport to restore all sewer systems that clogged the drainage system, causing flooding in some areas, especially along the national road. No. 21B, which is an important road for Kandal province as well as Takhmao city as a whole.
Kong Sophorn's order came as he led professional officers to inspect pumping stations and some areas flooded by rain in Takhmao City on the afternoon of September 7, 2021. This. At the same time, the provincial governor ordered all pumping stations to operate to pump water to release water in Takhmao City to reduce any risk that may occur eventually.
Mr. Meung Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, confirmed to Fresh Newss News Agency in Kandal Province that the main cause of the sewer blockage in Takhmao City was caused by sand clogging the sewer system. As a result, there is a blockage in the drainage.
He added that in accordance with the instructions of the Governor of Kandal Province, he organized a team to pump and restore sewers a week ago, so the flood situation is not so bad.
However, he also set out a number of plans to prepare for the restoration and release of water, including speeding up the four stations in Takhmao City, speeding up the pumping of water from Takhmao City. Drainage officials also rushed to pump sand out of the sewer system and restore the sewer to be clean.
Mr. Ming Yuleng requested that all heavy vehicles, including sand, stone, soil, gravel and heavy goods, be temporarily suspended from their traffic on Road 201, 209. , 108,109,110 and section 21 of the road from 7 to 15 September 2021 to avoid causing damage to the road rubber.
