Crack down like early rain! Six sand trucks fined and detained for one year for overweight
(Phnom Penh): Six more sand trucks were fined and detained for one year after overloading illegally. Five vehicles were stored at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport and one was stored at the Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport.
The six vehicles were intercepted and detained on September 6, 2021 by the Joint Mobile Task Force for Surveillance of Overweight Vehicles by the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Transport Vehicle Inspection Steering Committee. Overweight.
Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Task Force for the Suppression of Overweight Trucks, said that five sand trucks overweight from 15 to 22 tons were fined and detained for one year. Years due to loading more than 20% of the permitted weight in accordance with Article 60 of the Road Law.
The five vehicles were stopped on National Road 78 in O Kanseng village, Boeung Kanseng commune, Banlung district, Ratanakkiri province.
Separately, another heavy sand truck with a total weight of 70 tons loaded more than 30 tons. The car was fined and detained for one year at the Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport.
Please note that overweight trucks are one of the main causes of road damage. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has issued guidelines for strict implementation of these overweight trucks in accordance with the law, without exception. In addition to the legal fines, vehicles overweight of 20 percent or more will be stored for one year.
The team led by Mr. Seng Chhuon has been operating like rain in every provincial capital to intercept these overweight trucks. The overweight truck has been stopped and stored for several years.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol always called on the people who are transporters to abide by the law to avoid any penalties for traffic safety on the roads and to protect the roads from being damaged. Kampot Provincial Administration Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a Statue of Buddha Em Em Phuong
