Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab said that if we look at the last few years, we see the United States and China, or between the eagle and the dragon, acting like never before in the world. After the First Cold War came to an end. Anti-China politics has become a major focus of the United States, both militarily, economically and politically.
Rath Sandab continued that in the current context of the new economic war between the United States and China, or between the eagle and the dragon that are competing for control of the world in the 21st century. In this sense, if we look at the characteristics of each animal, we see that:
Eagle: A violent predator, eats fresh meat, eats hard, eats to win. What is remarkable is that eagles are powerful creatures that fly in the air and have a life expectancy of about 70 years.
But in order to survive until the age of 70, an eagle has to go through one of the most important decisions of its life, reaching the age of about 40. Its beak changes its shape, and it is unable to catch food or even claws. Its powerful toenails are long and tilted, making it impossible for it to catch prey. Not only that, but its wings are getting thicker and heavier, making it difficult for it to fly in search of food.
In general, there are many eagles that can go through the second method to become powerful animals, but also a large number that can not go through this painful stage and starve to death between the ages of 40. Years or to die in the midst of this transition.
Dragon: An animal that can live both in water and on land, a symbol of coolness, prosperity, religion, culture and business of the Chinese since the beginning. As for the Chinese philosophy, each family wants to be a dragon to show the superiority of their lineage.
In conclusion, Mr. Rath Sandab stated that if so, to the above question raised by the new economic war, can the dragon become the animal of the world?
