16 Siem Reap Macro Market Employees Found Positive Kovid 19
(Siem Reap): On September 4, 2021, yesterday, the Prasat Bakong District Authority, in cooperation with the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, inspected the location of Macro Market after finding 19 positive Kovid on 16 market employees.
The District Administrative Unity Command, in cooperation with the research team of the Provincial Health Department, inspected the condition of Macro Market, located in Kork Thnout Village, Kandek Commune, Prasat Bakong District, Siem Reap Province, and took samples from 242 Macro Market staff, 126 females.
During the quick test, 16 positive Kovid 19 were found, 13 of whom were female, and were taken to a medical center. As for the market, the District Administrative Unity Command did not close the location and allowed the business to continue to serve customers normally after the medical team inspected the safety in the market.
Mr. So Platon, Governor of Prasat Bakong District, informed the people who have been in and out of the above market place for the past 7 days to be isolated and self-immolate for 14 days in case of symptoms. For example, fever, sore throat, cough, tiredness, shortness of breath, please contact local authorities and working groups in villages and communes to get samples, test and receive proper treatment.
