ASEAN has been trying to end violence and political crisis in Myanmar and open peaceful dialogue between Myanmar's military leaders and the opposition after a coup overthrew Suu Kyi's government in February 2021. Erywan Yusof, Brunei's chief diplomat, was tasked with leading the effort last month.
"It is necessary for me to travel to Myanmar soon, but I think before doing so I need a guarantee," Eriwan told Reuters. "I have to be able to get a clear picture of what I have to do and what they will allow me to do when I visit."
According to Eriwan, he wants to visit Myanmar before the end of October, when ASEAN leaders will meet, but no specific date has been set. Eriwan said a request to meet with Aung San Suu Kyi had also been submitted to the Myanmar military.
