General Sao Sokha: The Armed Forces Fully Joins the Customs Institution to Raise National Funds on Law Enforcement of Vehicles with Cambodian and Cambodian License Plates
(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, confirmed that the National Gendarmerie has been fully cooperating with the Customs Institutions to raise funds for the national implementation. Law on private cars using license plates K.M. and N.P. by order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On the afternoon of September 4, 2021, General Sao Sokha emphasized that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's order was already in place on the occasion of the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Army. Some time ago, Samdech Techo instructed the Commander of the Armed Forces to cooperate with the Customs Institution, which is responsible for collecting revenue for the nation.
General Sao Sokha said that after receiving the strict order, he, as the Commander of the National Gendarmerie, also instructed and is continuing to monitor the performance of Gendarmerie officers throughout the country with the Customs. Apply the law to private cars that take refuge under the license plate K.M. and N.P. that do not pay proper taxes.
The Commander-in-Chief added that all members of the Armed Forces must be aware of their roles and responsibilities in educating and protecting law enforcement officers, namely customs officers. What is important is to crack down immediately in case any official or individual obstructs the implementation of the law by the customs officer on this revenue collection work.
General Sao Sokha also reminded all military officers not to forget their role in protecting security, order and defending the legitimate Royal Government resulting from the people's election. In addition, the Armed Forces also participated in the suppression of major crimes, including natural resource crimes and the rescue of people in natural disasters and other disasters.
General Sao Sokha recalled the four major slogans of the military: "The country must protect the people, must serve the law, must respect crime, must suppress." In case of any individual wrongdoing, the military must crack down and take action first.
Please be reminded that the Government of Cambodia has officially notified the Minister of the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Economy and Finance related to the implementation of the law on private vehicles, ministries, state institutions, especially the license plate K.M. and N.P. Enter to fulfill tax and import duties in accordance with laws and regulations on customs.
