Duke Leng Navatra is the son of a farmer living in Prey Veng province who has a poor standard of living. This family life situation is not conducive to childhood life to live in luxury, warmth, comfort and get a higher education.
The family situation also forced Duke Leng Navatra and his siblings to flee to South Korea in exchange for work to support their families. This difficult and poor life history is part of the motivation for him to participate in humanitarian activities in society.
For Duke Leng Navatra, wealth is only a temporary treasure when old age or life is exhausted and money cannot be taken with it. He considers his humanitarian activities to be a virtuous act in the society in return for the society and the people who have given him and his family the opportunity to build a better life.
Please note that Duke Leng Navatra, as well as his "Leng" family, have always shared difficulties with the Royal Government, such as the purchase of vaccines against Kovid 19, the fight against Kovid 19, and the relief from floods. The duke and his relatives have also been involved in other humanitarian activities, such as donating money to Kantha Bopha Hospital.
