Mr. Tith Mao, 60 years old, is a farmer who grows fragrant lentils on an area of about 8 hectares in Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province. Mr. Tith Mao has been growing lentils for 6 years. His gourds have been harvested for three years.
The fragrant gourd farmer pointed out that his first year gourd collection had a good market and the selling price was up to 8,000 riel, but gradually dropped to 4,500 riel. In the first year of harvesting, this fragrant lentil farmer received a total budget of about 40 million riels, and in the second year he received a total budget of about 75 million riels.
The Kovid 19 crisis left Tith Mao, as well as other farmers, with longan. This lack of marketing has led Mr. Tit Mao to be very worried and anxious.
But Tith Mao's worries and anxieties were allayed after he received information about the intervention of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in collecting his longan fruit as well as other farmers.
The purchase of longan fruits by Samdech Techo Prime Minister is not as high as the sales of farmers like last year. This has led some people to express negative and negative opinions about Samdech Techo's intervention.
But for the farmers who grow lentils themselves do not agree with the views of some people. Although the price is not as high as every year, Samdech Techo's intervention has helped to solve the problem better than leaving the ripe ones.
Mr. Tith Mao, as well as other farmers growing lentils and sorghum, in addition to being happy, they also expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit for collecting lentils as well as sorghum in the province. Battambang.
It should be noted that in order to solve the problem of longan market and longan fruit of farmers in Battambang and Pailin provinces, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit collected nearly 2,000 tons of longan fruit from farmers.
At present, the ripe fruit and fruit of the farmers are not yet ripe and are still ripening. Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit instructed Duke Leng Navatra to collect the lentils and raisins to distribute to the people at a low price (1900 Riel per kilogram) as a joint campaign to help Save the longan and turmeric fruit of Khmer farmers.
