WASHINGTON: The US Congress will discuss providing assistance to the United Nations (UN) and its agencies to provide humanitarian assistance to the Afghan people, but this aid will not be provided through a government-led government. By the Taliban. This was released by Reuters on Saturday morning, September 4, 2021.
The United States has been the largest donor to Afghanistan since the 2001 invasion that toppled the Taliban. So far, a total of $ 130 billion has been spent on security, governance, development and essential humanitarian assistance throughout Afghanistan.
According to Democrats, who now control both houses of Congress in the United States, the forthcoming humanitarian aid for Afghanistan will be aimed at helping Afghans fleeing, but not directly to the Taliban government. For the current situation.
The official, who spoke on condition of anonymity, said it would be "difficult" to persuade lawmakers to approve the aid if it fell into the hands of the Taliban and Republican lawmakers. There is no such day of consent. However, providing assistance through UN agencies is the best option for US lawmakers to consider in detail the costs.
