The Accounting and Auditing Regulator will start inspecting the implementation of accounting and auditing obligations for fines.
(Phnom Penh): The Accounting and Auditing Regulator on September 3, 2021 issued a notification on the inspection and implementation of transitional penalties for violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing and related regulations in force.
According to a statement obtained by Fresh News today, in accordance with the Law on Accounting and Auditing, enterprises are required to maintain accounting records, prepare financial statements in accordance with applicable accounting standards, submit financial statements to independent auditors, and Other relevant obligations as required by law.
Previously, the Ministry of Economy and Finance postponed the implementation of Sub-Decree No. 79 dated June 1, 2020 on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing for one year through Circular No. 007 Co. Dated September 11, 2020, and this extension will expire on September 11, 2021.
After the deadline as mentioned above, the Accounting and Auditing Regulators will start inspecting the implementation of accounting and auditing obligations and fines in case the Accounting and Auditing Regulators find that the enterprise has violated the Law on Accounting and Auditing and Letters. Relevant standards in force.
