Inspection Team of the Ministry of National Defense Resolves Dispute between Pump Station Owner and Residents in Kang Meas Village, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province
In response to the inspection team of the Ministry of National Defense, many people were also present. At that time, Nop Hoy, the chief of Kang Meas village, confirmed to the inspection team that he had just been the chief of Kang Meas village in 2019, so far it has been two years.
He never knew that there was a community of farmers using water in Kang Meas village, but when he became the village chief, he saw Ms. Ou Pen in charge of the pumping station and the main canal for pumping water from the lake to the main canal for the people. People use them for 300,000 riel per hectare.
He said that the pumping station, which includes a 500-meter-long main canal in Kang Meas village, is the achievement of PRASAC, which was built to pump water into the rice fields to irrigate the people. But many years ago, Ms. Ou Pen continued to manage this pumping station.
During the management of the station, Ms. Ou Pen also deleted a PRASAC main canal, nearly 500 meters long, without the knowledge of the authorities and officials. As for the water supply in the past, it was not enough to meet the needs of the people.
So Sambath, a 76-year-old resident of Kang Meas village, confirmed that the canal and the pumping station belonged to PRASAC. At that time, people used water from PRASAC free of charge.
And then the water pumped out of the lake falls into the main canal as high as the fields, people just cut the fields, the water flows into the fields without difficulty. But later, when Ms. Ou Pen took over, she kept deepening the canal to make it deeper than the rice fields, and when the people wanted to irrigate the rice fields, they had to get a pump from the main canal, but they had to pay 10 to 10 per machine. 150,000 Riels.
As for those who have far away fields, they have to pump out 300,000 riel per hectare from the foot of the crow. That is why they requested the competent Ministry authorities to help hand over the canal and the location of the above station to the people to use.
Ms. Ou Pen stated that she received control of the canal from the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology in 2011 after PRASAC abandoned it. At that time, there was nothing, she spent her own money to restore canals to pump water from the lake and dig many canals for people to install water pumps, earning a fee of 300,000 riel per hectare, because She also spent a lot of money.
But please do not accuse her of using the name of Phang Sophoeun as a national military police officer who is her husband to oppress the people is not right.
Dok Bunthon, director of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, told reporters on the afternoon of September 2 that the creation of a community or not is the same thing, everyone has the right to control. For a hectare of land, 300,000 riel is reasonable, and some places are more expensive. If accepted, they can all live together, because if there is no water manager, where will they get water to grow crops?
