He also informed the Ambassador about the Royal Government's efforts to control the spread of Kovid-19, especially the vaccination campaign for all Cambodians and foreigners, which is important for the rehabilitation. Socio-economic.
During the meeting, the Minister and Ambassador exchanged views on the progress of international trade in both bilateral and regional frameworks and discussed boosting trade volume between the two countries.
The talks noted the steady progress and continued agreement to further strengthen bilateral trade relations, especially the establishment of a free trade agreement between the two countries.
The Minister informed about the potential agricultural products of Cambodia which are in demand in the Indian market and requested the Indian side to increase investment in Cambodia, especially in the field of technology, infrastructure and increase the import of more agricultural machinery.
