International Event: Who is the Taliban in Afghanistan? While the first person leads the country, the second person leads the Ministry of Defense
After the Soviet expulsion, Afghanistan plunged into the chaos of the 1992 civil war, with mujahedeen commanders fighting to seize power and divide the capital, Kabul, one by one. In the civil war, a new movement, the Taliban, emerged under the leadership of Muhammad Umed in 1994 in Kandahar and began to gain more support from the Afghan people.
The Taliban have ruled Afghanistan for just over six years. On October 7, 2001, the United States, under former President George W. Bush, declared war on the Taliban after refusing to hand over and provide hiding places to al-Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden. Washington is accused of being behind the September 11, 2001 terrorist attacks.
