Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls for 8 Points to Continue Participating in Promoting Literacy
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, called for eight points to continue to contribute to the promotion of literacy in Cambodia more effectively. This is according to the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of the National Literacy Day on September 8, 2021, which was received by the media.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to continue to contribute to the promotion of literacy in Cambodia to be more effective, Samdech would like to call as follows:
* First, the relevant ministries and institutions must develop policies, legal frameworks, letters, norms and mechanisms necessary to lead, manage and implement effectively and quality to ensure lifelong learning for all citizens and in line with the new development objectives. Sustainable as well as socio-economic recovery after the Kovid 19 crisis.
* Second, all ministries, institutions, educational institutions, study centers, and pagodas must continue to develop lifelong educational programs in both literacy, vocational, and information technology to meet the needs of students.
* Third: Local authorities at all levels must pay more attention to support the development of learning center infrastructure and encourage people who do not study or drop out of school to have the opportunity to learn. In particular, we must strive to make it easier for people with disabilities to have access to equitable learning and an environment.
* Fifth: You are students in public and private educational institutions, Youth Union of Youth Federation of Cambodia, Youth Scouts and Youth of the Cambodian Red Cross must actively participate in volunteering to teach illiterate people in your community. Compatriots who are parents or guardians, please encourage your children to learn consistently and get good results for everyone.
* Sixth: Monasteries and temples must be mobilized by the movement of monks, clergy, and nuns to promote professional literacy programs by educating them about the importance of learning about morality and promoting a culture of citizenship. Global.
Seventh, development partners and non-governmental organizations must increase cooperation and strengthen partnerships with government institutions to support both resources and technology for all educational programs, especially literacy programs linked to vocational education to run smoothly. Regular.
* 8: Presidents of factories, enterprises and private companies, please encourage the opening of literacy classes, combined with vocational training for workers for their benefit and for the benefit of factory owners, we all need to Remember that "being literate, thinking and making the right decisions", "being literate leads to greater community development", "being literate, harmonizing the lives of individuals, families and society."
Taiwan claims China capable of disabling air defense system
Taiwan's Defense Ministry made the same conclusion in its annual report on the Chinese military submitted to the National Assembly. "China could launch cyber-attacks against the global cyber network, which could cause them to shut down or freeze our air defense system, and this could be a major threat to us," the report said. .
According to the Taiwanese Ministry of Defense, China has rapidly developed intelligence capabilities through the Beidou satellite system, which China uses to build its own GPS system against the United States. This means that Beijing can monitor or monitor all activities around Taiwan with the help of reconnaissance planes, drones, and reconnaissance ships.
One public official in Svay Rieng province must retire early, while five other officials have been demoted and relocated after issuing a driver's license without exam.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has decided to retire one official early, while five other officials have been relocated and demoted because they made mistakes in issuing driver's licenses to citizens. Without the applicant coming to the exam. This is according to the decision of the Minister of Public Works and the Governor of Svay Rieng Province, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of September 1, 2021.
According to the above, Mr. Prum Pho, who is the Director of the Office of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Svay Rieng Province and the Chairman of the Driving License Examination Commission, has been retired before the due date due to his salary and other allowances. It must be removed from the payroll from September 1, 2021.
With the punishment of his officials after misbehaving, Kong Vimean, the director of the cabinet and the spokesman of the Ministry, added that in this case, the sub-national administration has enforced disciplinary changes for these officials. One, Prum Pho, retired prematurely and five other officials moved from their old positions to a new one with a demotion.
He added that "the position of the Ministry led by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol will continue to apply if in the provinces dare to act like the case in Svay Rieng will be able to reach even more severe punishment."
