Officials: More and more people turn their attention to securities trading, more than 3,000 new trading accounts opened in 8 months
(Phnom Penh): The public seems to be more interested in trading on the stock market because they know more about the Cambodia Securities Exchange after receiving training and perceive that trading can be profitable, starting with a small amount of capital. .
"During the last few years, there has been a lot of public outcry over the actual trading accounts. In 2020, there were 4,266 trading accounts, and in 2021, there will be 3,077 trading accounts," he said. Account as of August. Since the launch of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, there have been 30,237 trading accounts.
"The reason for opening more accounts is because they understand more about the securities sector through the flow of training," he said. On the other hand, the public believes that the securities sector can be profitable, investment is easy and start investing with little capital, and believes that in the next 3-5 years, there will be more companies to list and issue more securities. "Make investment more attractive."
He added that the public is more interested because the big bank in Cambodia, ACLEDA Bank, has listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, which is one of the keys to attracting the public. Even so, owning one is still beyond the reach of the average person.
The Cambodia Securities Exchange has been actively involved in disseminating knowledge about trading, various investments in the securities sector to the general public. In fact, in the past, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has always organized workshops to share knowledge to the public, even though it is now in the context of Kovid 19 disease, it also continues its activities through live Facebook Page.
In that, the Cambodia Securities Exchange opened lectures and answered questions directly on its Facebook Page once a week and every Friday at 3:00 pm. Under various topics such as: listed company forum to allow investors to meet directly with listed companies to get the latest information on business and future plans. Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority earns about $ 40 million in the first half
