Heavy rains cause runoff to affect crops and homes in Sampov Loun and Phnom Proek districts
(Battambang): Rain continued to fall for many hours, causing flash floods, landslides, affecting crops, property, roads and houses of many people in Sampov Loun and Phnom Proek districts on the evening of August 31, 2021 In the past.
District authorities and authorities confirmed that heavy rains continued for several hours, covering several areas, including Sampov Loun and Phnom Preuk districts, Battambang province, causing severe damage to many crops, including roads. Housing and some other property.
The effects of the rain yesterday evening affected and threatened in a total of 5 communes in Sampov Loun and Phnom Prek districts in the western part of Battambang province. The above five communes were damaged, including Sampov Loun commune, which affected 2 rai of cassava fields of farmers and 2 rai of red corn plantations.
In Santepheap commune, water leaked and flooded, causing damage to the fence of O'Chum Udom Samaki pagoda, 30 meters long, completely collapsed, with a total budget of 6,000 US dollars, especially in Phnom Proek district, affecting the roads and houses of the people. Many of the three communes are Phnom Proek, Barang Tluak and Buor.
The heavy rains also affected some other districts in the border, such as Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province.
