Minister of Commerce: Cambodia benefits from belt and road project
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that Cambodia has received many benefits from the belt and road project, which will contribute to the development of Cambodia in the future.
Mr. Pan Sosak said this while participating as the guest speaker at the 6th Belt and Road Initiative Summit on the Promotion of Multilateral Cooperation. The meeting was held via remote video on Wednesday, September 1, 2021.
The meeting aims to strengthen multilateral cooperation under the China Belt and Road Initiative with partner countries including ASEAN, the World Trade Organization (WTO) and other trade partners in the bilateral, regional and multilateral contexts. .
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak confirmed the ASEAN-Cambodia economic recovery plan in the context of the 19-post and post-crisis Kovid crisis. In particular, ensuring the flow of essential goods, medical equipment and food.
In connection with the Belt and Road Project, Mr. Pan Sosak emphasized that Cambodia has been benefiting greatly from the Belt and Road Initiative, which contributes to infrastructure development. In particular, structures in the transport sector include bridges, dams, airports, seaports and rivers.
"These developments will lead to enhancing Cambodia's trade facilitation and competitiveness, which will lead to development, economic growth, population well-being and poverty eradication." This is the confirmation of Mr. Pan Sosak.
At today's meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to continue to work closely with the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region and its regional and global trading partners to boost trade and economic growth. .
