Senior Minister Sun Chanthol tells students that work must be connected with the heart to be effective
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, told students studying at the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport that all work, even with specific skills, is associated with love and sharp will. More to make the work more effective.
On August 31, 2021, Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport organized a talk between students and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to provide some behavioral advice and education as additional capital for students to live in society. As well as for various tasks.
During the meeting, there was also the invitation of Preah Panha Monianhan Hak Shanghai, Executive Director of the Buddhist Organization for Education of Cambodia to provide some education to students on the path of Dharma. Venerable Hak Shenghai gave advice focusing on the relationship between knowledge and behavior for students and intellectuals.
The Venerable Sangha said that students and intellectuals who have only knowledge, skills, but lack morality and virtue are like Bopha who lack kanthapidor, and all knowledge that lacks moral values is easily harmful to society. Nation and the whole world.
For Venerable Hak Shenghai, he wants to see students who study at the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport apply their knowledge and skills to work in society and the country, adhere to virtue, so that everything they do has value for humanity. .
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol expressed his full support for Venerable Hak Shanghai. During the meeting, the Senior Minister also provided some additional advice to educate and educate students on ethics.
The senior minister also reminded all students who are studying when leaving work to do it carefully, from the heart and heart to make the job better.
"If we do not have the work in our hearts, we do not have the will to work, we will not be effective," he said. So we have to do everything to make it quality and do it right once, not twice. But we do it twice and waste time and money. "If you build a road, make it a quality road, do not build it and come and rebuild it again and again, it is a waste of time for us, the people and the national budget."
"When we do something, especially our road work, we have to consider the road users," he said. We do it for the people who use the road, but have to think that our actions can cause accidents or not? "Everything we do needs to be clear to our road users."
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also instructed the students to make efforts to study and acquire knowledge and skills to help the society without embarrassing or damaging the value of the institute. In addition, it is necessary to take knowledge and skills to help develop the country to be more prosperous.
He said the idea was not to live on a wealthy island surrounded by poor seas. Help dig up this rich island and make the poor sea as small as possible for the Cambodian people and people all over the world.
