Ministry of Commerce: Cambodia's exports to Japan reached nearly $ 600 million in the first 7 months of this year!
(Phnom Penh): In the first seven months of 2021, Cambodia exported to Japan in the amount of 597 million dollars, an increase of 0.95 percent, while imports from Japan in the amount of 348 million dollars. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia.
According to the report, the trade volume between the two countries in the first seven months of 2021 reached a total of 945 million US dollars, down 2.73% compared to the same period in 2020 of 972 million US dollars.
Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News on September 1, 2021 that at present, despite the crisis of the 19-Kovid crisis, trade flows between Cambodia and Japan Still behaving normally.
In 2020, Cambodia exported more than $ 1 billion to Japan, while imports from Japan to Cambodia amounted to more than $ 637 million.
As of July 2021, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has decided to allow Japanese companies to invest in a total of 211 projects under a total investment of 3,140 million US dollars.
