Head of Royal Government of Cambodia issues sub-decree to establish Bou Vil commune, Bavel district, Battambang province
According to the sub-decree of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Bou Vil commune has 9 villages: Bavel 2 village, Tumnup Teuk village, Prey Toteung 1 village, Prey Toteung 2 village, Kork village, Sl Khlanh village, Kampong Chhnang 1 village, Kampong Chhnang 2 village and Samaki village, excluding Bavel commune. Cambodian Ambassador to Australia warns Cambodians to be wary of recruitment information for Australia under the new "Agriculture" visa scheme
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Australia on September 1, 2021 issued a notice informing Cambodians to be careful of all information on recruitment to work in Australia under the visa scheme. New "agriculture" as the project is currently being discussed by the Australian Government (Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Ministry of Agriculture).
In this case, in order to avoid being deceived by crooks, the Embassy would like to clarify that the Australian Government (Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Ministry of Agriculture and the Australian Ministry of Agriculture) is currently discussing the preparation of a "new agricultural" visa scheme with various conditions. To obtain this visa.
The new visa scheme will be finalized by the end of September 2021. The Australian government will also hold bilateral talks with a number of regional partners on the new visa scheme.
The Embassy would also like to inform you that under the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to find a job market for Cambodian workers, the Embassy has tried to find a job market for Cambodians in Australia as well as New Zealand through meetings with leaders. Of each country's government.
For this new agricultural visa project, under the guidance of the leadership of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the support of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia, the Embassy is ready to continue to meet the Cambodian government with the Australian Government to negotiate labor markets. .
The Embassy would like to reiterate that the Agricultural Visa Project is currently in the process of being prepared and the Australian Government has not yet decided whether to grant this type of visa to Cambodia or any other country. Therefore, the Embassy would like to ask you to be very careful about any information about the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to work in Australia by any recruitment agency.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, has recommended four points to encourage the private sector in Cambodia to use digital technology in business operations to expand the market.
The encouragement of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth was made during the invitation to participate in the official launch of the business registration system for information technology nurseries, the second phase, held on September 1, 2021.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that the private sector has been playing an important role in starting to digitalize its business through the use of digital technology in business operations and as a way to expand its market. Online shopping and e-commerce.
He also announced that the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant ministries and institutions, will launch a national support program for small and medium enterprises to embrace digital technology, which is comprehensive and comprehensive. "Financial, technical and professional aspects."
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on September 1, 2021, confirmed that for more than a year, from June 15, 2020 to As of August 24, 2021, 7,715 companies have registered business in information technology nurseries with a total capital of nearly 3 billion US dollars.
This statement was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, officially launched the second phase of the Information Technology Nursery Business Registration System via video this morning. September 1, 2021.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated, “Over the past one year, the business registration system has been running smoothly and has allowed businesses to apply for business registration anytime and anywhere as of the 24th of this month. In August 2021, the total number of companies registered in the information technology nursery was 7,715 and the total capital was nearly 3 billion US dollars.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, the Royal Government of Cambodia officially launched the first phase of information technology business registration system on June 15, 2020, with high interest and enthusiasm from the private sector. The system also contributed significantly to the sustainability of economic activity in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that this underscores the importance and necessity of the use of digital systems to support the provision of public services, especially in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis.
Please note that the business registration system for information technology nurseries is a sharp reform package of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, presented at the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum on March 29. 2019 ago.
In the first phase, the system covered the business registration of the Ministry of Commerce, the tax registration of the General Department of Taxation and the issuance of the opening announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and was officially launched. June 15, 2020.
In particular, in the second phase, the system will expand the scope to apply for licenses or permits online according to business activities from ministries - professional institutions with the role of technical supervision in the field.
Four ministries and institutions participated in the second phase, including the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, and the real estate and mortgage regulators of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority.
