(Phnom Penh): The Commander of the 5th Army Division, Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, has issued an order to the troops stationed along the Cambodian-Thai border to strictly prevent the smuggling of right-hand drive vehicles through the corridors along the border.
In the order received by Fresh News on September 1, Lt. Gen. Sam Oun emphasized that the prevention of the import of right-hand drive vehicles is in accordance with the request of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. Cambodia on August 4.
In this order, Lt. Gen. Sam Oun also pointed out that any soldier who conspired to smuggle right-hand drive vehicles through the corridors along the border in violation of this decision, the unit commander will face the law.
The Commander of the 5th Army Division also instructed the Commanders of the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th Divisions to disseminate this order to the commanders of all units in the area under their responsibility.
It should be noted that on August 4, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, wrote a letter requesting Samdech Techo Hun Sen to decide on some measures for cars with license plates. As well as right-hand drive vehicles.
The proposal also states that the import tax and import duties on right-hand drive vehicles will be available locally for the last time by the end of June 2022. But the steering wheel must be changed from right to left to legalize Cambodia's road traffic. After that, the right-hand drive vehicle that is suppressed will be required to be disassembled or destroyed.
