Following is a press release from the Pailin Provincial Administration: A regional conference on the development of alternative training model adapted to the academic context of universities in the Asia-Pacific region was held online.
(Phnom Penh): Regional Conference on "Development of Model Training by Adaptation Adapted to the Academic Context of Universities in the Asia-Pacific" Organized by the French Higher Education Agency AUF in collaboration with the University of Economics Of Ho Chi Minh City on August 31, 2021 online.
About 300 university leaders, university professors, researchers and economists and training professionals from many countries in the region, including Vietnam, Laos, Thailand, Mongolia, Vanuatu, New Caledonia, etc. Participated in this forum.
Speaking at the opening of the event, Mr. SLIM Khalbous, Rector of the Agency for Higher Education in the French Language, stated that Asia is undergoing profound changes that are evident through the education and training of higher education institutions. Education is an important factor in economic development, focusing on quality in particular.
He said that in order to achieve this goal, vocational training in many countries has linked three main players: students who will become future employees, open universities to the private sector and companies that are future employers. Of young people who will enter the job market.
In this regard, the AUF has mobilized resources and knowledge from the sources of Francophone science, which the AUF has built into a global network to support education systems and higher education institutions on employment issues to provide opportunities for young people. Will graduate better.
It should be noted that this one-morning conference focuses on model training at some higher education institutions in Asia and other regions, in collaboration with the private sector on the development of alternate training programs between theoretical studies at institutions. Study and practice or practice in the company.
It is a training that adapts to the actual needs of the private sector. The speakers talked about building the foundation of study and integration of university programs and some examples of collaborative training with industry in the Hanoi Polytechnic Institute.
This alternative training has been developed in recent years by a number of institutions in the region that demonstrate significant efficiency and effectiveness in the job market. To this end, the AUF has established the Francophone Job Center (CEF), which will propose short-term skills training programs. The CEF is also a meeting place for exchanges between universities and socio-economic actors. A
