WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Joe Biden on Tuesday fully defended his decision to withdraw US troops from Afghanistan. The president also told the American people that he would never send the next generation to such an endless war. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday morning, September 1, 2021.
According to Joe Biden, the United States spent more than $ 2.3 trillion on the 20-year war in Afghanistan and killed more than 2,400 soldiers. In the end, however, the Taliban were able to return to power.
On Tuesday, the Taliban and pro-Taliban people in Kabul took to the streets and chanted what they called "Afghanistan's freedom and success." The Taliban immediately deployed forces to take control of Hamid Karzai International Airport and also claimed that negotiations to form a new government were in the final stages.
China sees complete withdrawal of US troops as new chapter in Afghanistan
BEIJING: The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Tuesday announced that the complete withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan is a turning point for the South Asian nation and the worst possible end to the unrest. Of air evacuation at Kabul International Airport. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday morning, September 1, 2021.
The Chinese Foreign Ministry has repeatedly criticized the sudden withdrawal of troops by the United States, and China has said it is ready to establish friendly relations and cooperation with the Taliban. Deeper.
