The following is the announcement: Ministry of Water Resources: From today to September 7, rain will continue to fall from medium to high, some areas may be flooded, please be careful of natural phenomena!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia from today to September 7, 2021.
During the coming weeks, Cambodia will be severely affected by the Indian low pressure valley with a low pressure system, and on September 2 and 4, an additional effect will be Breeze Sea breeze, the ministry said.
Such a situation will cause the provinces in the central lowlands and provinces bordering the Dangrek Mountains and the northeastern highlands to receive moderate to heavy rain mixed with thunder and gusts, and some areas may experience flash floods.
For coastal provinces, moderate to heavy rain is expected, mixed with thunder, lightning and gusts. In the sea, especially near the islands, sea waves will occur at a moderate level.
At the same time, the Ministry of Water Resources called on people to be careful of natural phenomena that may occur eventually. During the 31 days of the vaccination campaign for children and adolescents aged 12 to 17 years, 1,553,114 doctors were vaccinated
