WASHINGTON, Aug. 31 (Xinhua) - August 31, 2021, is the date on which the United States will withdraw all its troops from Afghanistan by order of President Joe Biden. Indeed, the withdrawal plan was carried out under the administration of former US President Donald Trump, who sent his officials to hold several rounds of talks with the Taliban in Doha, Qatar, in 2020.
The following is the beginning of the most bitter US war in Afghanistan in 20 years:
Of the 19 hijackers, not a single Afghan was identified, with 15 reported to be Saudi nationals. In the aftermath of the attack, former US President George W. Bush vowed to win the war on terror and called on the Taliban government to "surrender all al Qaeda leaders to the United States, otherwise they will not be free." Absolutely. ”
September 18, 2001 - President George W. Bush signs a joint resolution to become law on the use of force against those behind the September 11, 2001 attacks on the United States. . The joint resolution was later confirmed by the Bush administration as a legitimate reason for the United States to decide to wage war on terror, invade Afghanistan, eavesdrop on the American people without a court order.
June 2002 - Hamid Karzai, who has been the head of Afghanistan's interim administration since December 2001, is appointed head of Afghanistan's interim government. The appointment was made during an emergency meeting in Kabul attended by 1,550 delegates.
In January 2004, a group of 502 Afghan delegates agreed to establish a constitution for Afghanistan, deciding to establish a presidential system. The move is seen by the United States and its Western allies as a positive step toward democracy.
October 29, 2004 - Al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden first appears in a video released just three weeks after Afghanistan's election and just days before George W. Bush was elected. President again in his second term. In the video, which aired on Al Jazeera television, Osama bin Laden mocked the Bush administration and claimed responsibility for the September 11, 2001 attacks.
On May 23, 2005, Afghan President Hamid Karzai and US President George W. Bush issued a joint statement declaring the two countries' strategic partnership. Through this statement, the United States has the right to use the Afghan military infrastructure as well as to help train the Afghan army.
On September 18, 2005, more than 6 million Afghans participated in the parliamentary elections, considered one of the largest democratic elections ever in Afghanistan. That is, more than half of the participants in this election are women.
On February 17, 2009, then-US President Barack Obama announced plans to send thousands more troops to the war zone, focusing on Afghanistan, which he considers a key partner. Of the United States in the fight against terrorism. As of January 2009, the United States had more than 37,000 troops stationed in Afghanistan.
On March 27, 2009, President Barack Obama announced a new strategic plan linking success in Afghanistan to stability in Pakistan. Through this plan, the United States aims to eradicate and destroy al Qaeda asylum in Pakistan and prevent terrorists from leaving Pakistan for Afghanistan.
In July 2009, the US Marine Corps launched an offensive operation in southern Afghanistan as a major test of a new US military strategy against the Taliban. The new strategy involves more than 4,000 US Marines as the Taliban progresses, especially in Helmand province.
In November 2010, at a summit in Lisbon, Portugal, NATO member states signed a statement agreeing to hand over full responsibility for security in Afghanistan to Afghan forces in Afghanistan. At the end of 2014. The decision paves the way for the US and NATO to gradually withdraw from Afghanistan.
June 22, 2011 - President Barack Obama announces plans to reduce the number of US troops in Afghanistan by more than 3,000 before the summer of 2012. Obama's decision comes after opinion polls show that the majority of Americans do not support the United States' continued war abroad.
In January 2012, the Taliban set up a representative office in Qatar to pave the way for talks with the United States. But two months later, the Taliban canceled all talks with the United States, accusing Washington of failing to keep its promises of a prisoner exchange and stepping up attacks on foreign troops in Afghanistan.
On May 27, 2014, President Barack Obama announced the date for the withdrawal of most US troops from Afghanistan before 2016. Many experts at the time saw Barack Obama's decision as part of a shift in focus to Asia, where China's influence was growing.
On August 21, 2017, Donald Trump made some speeches that made it clear that he intended to continue the war in Afghanistan. Mr. Trump has said that the decision to withdraw US troops depends on the actual situation, not on the timing of the withdrawal.
In January 2018, the Taliban launched a series of attacks in Kabul that killed more than 115 people as the Trump administration launched a plan to deploy US troops to rural areas. Across Afghanistan, to advise the Afghan army on leading airstrikes, destroying opium poppy fields, a source of income for the Taliban.
The agreement between the United States and the Taliban did not include a ceasefire, and days after the signing, Taliban fighters launched an offensive against the Afghan army. In response, the United States has launched airstrikes on the Taliban in Helmand province.
On April 14, 2021, US President Joe Biden announced the withdrawal of the remaining 3,500 US troops from Afghanistan before August 31. Just before the anniversary of the September 11, 2001 terrorist attacks, did not follow the date agreed upon by Trump and Lebanon.
But Biden defended his decision, saying the withdrawal was the end of the US-end war in Afghanistan and that the real goal was to successfully assassinate al-Qaeda-bin Laden.
On August 26, 2021, 13 US soldiers were killed in an ISIS suicide bombing at Kabul airport, and the Biden administration continues to evacuate US citizens and troops from Afghanistan. Before the deadline is August 31 this week.
The United States has temporarily suspended its diplomatic mission in Kabul from August 30, 2021 and transferred it to Qatar.
The resolution, drafted by the United States, the United Kingdom and France, was approved by 13 of the 15 members of the UN Security Council, with no objections, while China and Russia abstained.
Under the resolution, the UN Security Council expects the Taliban to allow as well as ensure that foreigners and Afghans can continue to leave Afghanistan safely if they choose to leave.
Tuesday, August 31, 2021 is the date that US President Joe Biden has set for US troops to leave Afghanistan completely. The last US military flight left Afghanistan on Monday night, one day ahead of schedule.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has rejected some of the criticism that Cambodia is dependent on China to build infrastructure.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol announced this on August 30, 2021 on the occasion of being the guest speaker at the MPWT LIVE SHOW under the theme "Road Infrastructure Achievements from the end of 2018 to the present and the plan is continuing until 2023 "with the participation of relevant leaders and officials.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "I would like to reject the criticism that Cambodia relies on China to build various infrastructure systems. Cambodia does not discriminate in funding sources for the construction of roads and bridges in Cambodia, that is, Cambodia does not deny "Any friendly country that wants to help Cambodia if it provides timely assistance or loans to build roads and bridges."
The senior minister added that the loan procedure from one country to another varies, some countries take 3 to 5 years to study the construction project and agree to borrow money, so if we wait 5 years, we will lose a lot of income. Construction of roads and bridges.
He also stressed the importance of road and bridge infrastructure to contribute to economic development, especially national integration, transportation of goods and tourism, and reiterated the wise recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has said since 1985 that in order to build a motherland, we must have: roads, electricity, water and human resources.
In addition, the Senior Minister informed the progress of the Kratie-Kampong Thom bridge project, which is an important bridge project that will enable people to travel directly from Kratie to Kampong Thom and save travel time. The bridge project has been fully negotiated and a bridge construction agreement has already been signed, with the hope that the bridge project can open the construction site later this year or early January 2022 after signing the loan. .
The instruction of the Ministry of Education states that during the suspension of the educational institution due to the community event of February 20, 2021, the educational institution carried out teaching and distance learning in all forms, including teaching and learning in groups. Learn together on a small scale between teachers and students in a safe place.
Pursuant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry would like to introduce some important principles to the Capital-Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Office of Education, Youth and Sports of Municipal, District, Khan Administration, all public and private educational institutions, parents, guardians, students. On teaching and learning in colleges in low-risk geographical institutions as follows:
First, the reopening of general education institutions at all levels in low-risk municipalities, districts and Khans by the Capital and Provincial authorities must assess the actual situation and the implementation of safety gaps and necessary health measures.
* Must continue to implement the curriculum
Second, continuing education in groups of less than 15 and shifting or mixed learning in urban areas and cities that are less contagious and already vaccinated.
* Evaluate the study area to prepare the learning and teaching mechanism and make a clear plan with the approval of the Capital and Provincial Authority and send it to the Ministry for summary * Establish a school management committee with the participation of parents and local authorities To provide information
* Prioritize 9th and 12th grade students to study in schools, but in the form of group learning with less than 15 students and take turns to facilitate teaching and management
* Divide the teachers into responsibilities according to the cluster or at each grade level (in case the teacher is unable to coordinate, the senior students are arranged in the cluster together or the parents help the younger students)
* Must continue to apply mixed learning methods
- Continuing learning in a variety of ways, such as learning online, distributing documents, and learning in the classroom, taking turns in groups and improving hygiene on a regular basis. Tutorials and worksheets produced by the specialized departments of the Ministry and distributed via telegram, website, or mobile applications
- Continuing to practice mixed and electronic teaching, with teachers being able to teach live and provide opportunities for students to self-study using textbooks and electronically, conducting tests and assessments of students, especially classes. 9th and 12th to be complete under the picture as a monthly, quarterly, annual scoring test
* Shrink curriculum implementation
- Weekly and monthly re-planning of lessons by focusing on the main lesson content that is the basis for further study in the next grade - Summarize the lesson content by focusing on the rules that make it easy for students to understand and apply Yes - Encourage and assist students to do homework or do additional training at home - Other subjects are suspended and will be supplemented at the beginning of the next school year
Third: Online distance learning and learning for high-risk geography
* Continuing teaching and learning electronically and distributing documents
* Continuing to practice mixed and electronic teaching, with teachers being able to teach live and provide students with the opportunity to self-study using textbooks and e-learning.
Perform all tests and assessments of students, especially 9th and 12th grade, under the guise of monthly, quarterly, and annual scoring tests.
* For high-risk geography, home study groups can be arranged, field trips selected by the community and district authorities, and self-study groups by high school students to help lower grade students.
* For high-risk geography, parental or guardian consent is required and parental involvement is required, and worksheets must be followed.
* Encourage parents to encourage and create distance learning and self-study for students, especially young students.
Fourth, strengthening health protection measures for educators, students, especially teachers over the age of 50, and preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease:
* The management of the educational institution must inspect, take care of, and improve the hygiene and order in the school, even if the educational institution has not reopened yet.
* No sale of food or snacks and sports activities on campus
Fifth, the establishment of a school management committee with the participation of parents and local authorities to decide at the school level to open or suspend schools. Svay Rieng Provincial Administration Introduces Urgent Measures to Control and Prevent the Spread of Tuberculosis in Cattle
(Svay Rieng): The Svay Rieng Provincial Administration on August 31, 2021 issued guidelines on emergency measures to control and prevent the spread of cattle skin diseases to the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Provincial Information Department. Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Gendarmerie, Provincial Military Operation Area, Governor of 8 districts.
Cattle mumps is a viral disease that is currently spreading in many provinces in Cambodia, especially in Svay Rieng province from June to August 2021, the number of animal mumps is more than. 1,000 in seven districts, which is a high risk of a large-scale epidemic that has a serious impact on the economy of farmers, livestock and the economy of the province.
The virus can be transmitted from one animal to another through direct or indirect contact with infected animals, such as vampires, flies, mosquitoes, frogs, bats, food transport, semen, freezing the environment and other infectious agents. More.
The pathogen is environmentally resistant, can live in dry skin for up to 3 months and up to 6 months in cages, dirty and without enough light, can live in pH from 6.3 to 8.3. It is easy to die from sunlight, high acidity, high base and stop activity at temperatures of 55 degrees Celsius and above, and easy to get rid of with soapy water.
In order to effectively prevent and prevent the spread of the above diseases, Svay Rieng Provincial Administration would like to introduce to the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Provincial Information Department, Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Gendarmerie, Provincial Military Operations Area, 8 District Governors and All relevant authorities must implement the following specific measures:
* Second, the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Military Operations Area and relevant authorities at the border must strengthen inspections of all live cattle, frozen sperm and imported beef products must have a sanitary certificate from the country. Exported and subjected to animal health inspections and catalysis by veterinary officers.
* Third: The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries must educate the people, village animal health agencies, local cattle breeders, farms, farms to maintain, provide water, feed, health monitoring and proper implementation of biosafety rules. Technique.
* Fourth: The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the district administration must disseminate in all forms to the people and cattle farmers to understand the impact and serious damage to animal production in the economy caused by skin tumors. The cattle.
* Fifth, the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Provincial Information Department shall widely disseminate to farmers and stakeholders on the provincial radio about the contents of this instruction and technical articles on measures to prevent and treat gonorrhea. Buffalo.
* Sixth: Authorities at all levels, departments and relevant units must jointly examine and find solutions to any problems that hinder the implementation of this instruction, as well as provide information to the provincial administration by all means to examine and find solutions in a timely manner. Time and efficiency. Chbar Ampov District Governor Visits and Presents Gifts to Preah Ponlea Village Chief
