Mr. Pan Sosak told officials that solving challenges and finding markets for Cambodian products is necessary
(Phnom Penh): In front of his professional officials, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, emphasized that finding markets and solving challenges for Cambodian products is a priority and must be given the highest priority.
The Minister said this during the first meeting of the working group to solve challenges and promote the sale of Cambodian products in the country and export on August 30.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak highlighted that in order to promote product sales and address challenges for Cambodian products, the Ministry of Commerce has set out several key mechanisms and strategies.
The Minister of Commerce said that through this mechanism, the Ministry of Commerce has set up a working group to address challenges more smoothly and effectively to promote the sale of Cambodian products in both domestic and export markets. Go abroad more widely.
In yesterday's meeting, the Minister also gave some recommendations to the working group to guide the implementation of marketing and solving challenges for this Cambodian product more effectively. Recommended recommendations include:
Strictly implement the recommendations and especially the results of the discussions. In this context, all members of the working group have experience in going through and resolving issues during the time of the Kovid-19 crisis, and the market environment has evolved rapidly. (Especially market prices) caused by the uncertainty of the epidemic crisis and the competition of economic powers
* The main objectives of this working group are to: (1) Assist farmers in selling their products in both domestic and export markets (2) Assisting consumers To obtain quality goods at better prices; and (3) assisting businesses and businesses to be able to trade smoothly and competitively in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
In addition, Mr. Pan Sosak reminded the team that the work of finding markets and solving challenges for Cambodian products is an important task that relevant officials must pay the highest attention.
