The following is the announcement of the Ministry of National Defense: KOICA trains Cambodian officials on "Improving the administration of judicial administration in Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia has launched a training program on "Improving the Management of Judicial Administration in Cambodia" for 25 Cambodian officials from the Ministry of Justice and the General Department. Judicial administration.
The training was conducted online for 12 days from September 6 to 17, 2021. The purpose of this training is to improve and modernize the judicial administration system in Cambodia and to strengthen the capacity of court officials to formulate judicial administration policies electronically.
This important training course is designed to: First, provide references to Korea's experience in the field of law and justice in Cambodia, Second: Assist in the improvement and modernization of the judiciary, and third. : Strengthen the responsibility and understanding of the ethics of law and court officials.
In addition, participants will create an action plan that incorporates knowledge from learning, discussion, experience and exploration during the program. The action plan is the main activity of the program, which gives participants the opportunity to write actionable and feasible action plans to provide options as well as solutions to issues raised in the country report.
In Cambodia, KOICA works on a variety of technical aspects of programs and projects that have a significant impact on Cambodia's development, such as improving nutrition and student well-being, capacity building of teachers, public health, agriculture, and infrastructure. Innovative ship.
