(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has cooperated with the private sector and stakeholders to implement a new project "Promoting the internal tourism movement and promoting community-based tourism activities in the context of Kovid-19 disease", which aims to restore and develop the tourism community in particular. It helps communities to create new businesses and expand existing ones, contributing to the recovery of the local economy.
This cooperation will be implemented after the morning of Friday, August 27, 2021, at the Ministry of Tourism, a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed between the Ministry of Tourism and Cambodian entrepreneurs on the project "Promoting the internal tourism movement and promoting tourism activities in the community. In the context of Kovid-19 disease.
The signing ceremony was attended by Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of the General Department of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, and Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Khmer Entrepreneurship, under the testimony of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Strategy, ready for economic recovery. From Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance
This collaborative project focuses on promoting tourism to key tourism communities in four target provinces: Siem Reap, Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang, with priority given to key activities such as providing training on essential skills. Some include community entrepreneurship training, community outreach videos, community signage, and collaboration with the private sector to promote the community.
Mr. Thong Khon said that ecotourism and community tourism are sub-sectors of world tourism that remain active and operational even during the Kovid-19 crisis, especially supporting domestic tourism activities and being an effective tool for promoting development. At the base.
The Minister said that the development of a tourism and ecotourism community of strategic and political character has really contributed significantly to local development, especially promoting the participation of the people in the process of national development through empowerment. Empower them to directly manage and develop their community (Local Empowerment).
In this regard, the cooperation between the Ministry of Tourism and Cambodian entrepreneurs will now contribute to the socio-economic benefits of local people directly in the community through tourism in the context of Kovid-19 disease, as well as the maintenance, protection and conservation of resources. Nature and cultural heritage preserve the original identity of the local community.
The Ministry of Tourism is optimistic about the project and expects Cambodian entrepreneurs to become potential partners with the Ministry of Tourism in promoting the development of community-based tourism and ecotourism sub-sectors and tourism in general. Another 436 vehicles were inspected and fined on August 30, 2021
