The following is the press release of Koh Kong Provincial Administration: The Ministry of Labor warns citizens to be very careful about all the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to work in Australia by any recruitment agency or unit.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on August 30, 2021, announced to the Cambodian people to be very careful about all the recruitment and sending of Cambodian workers to work in Australia by any recruitment agency or unit.
Taking this opportunity, the Ministry would like to confirm that Sub-Decree No. 190 dated 17 August 2011 on the Management of the Sending of Cambodian Workers Abroad through Private Recruitment Agencies determines that workers refer to Cambodian citizens of both sexes who are in All stages of labor migration, from the time of signing the employment service contract with the recruitment agency until the time of repatriation.
At the same time, it also includes Cambodians of both sexes who go to internship and work abroad and have a valid contract recognized by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. At the same time, the sub-decree also states that "the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is the Ministry responsible for managing the sending of Cambodian workers abroad in cooperation with the relevant ministries and institutions."
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will continue to work with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in negotiations with the Australian Government to accept Cambodian migrant workers under the Australian Agricultural Visa. The ministry will provide more information on the detailed terms and procedures after discussions with the Australian government.
