(Phnom Penh): As of July 2021, the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) has decided to allow Japanese companies to invest in a total of 211 projects under a total investment of 3,140 million US dollars.
The investment figures were presented in a press release of the 22nd meeting of the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee on video on August 30.
"As of July 2021, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has decided to allow 145 Japanese companies to invest outside the SEZ with a total investment of 2.8 billion US dollars. In 66 special economic zones, the total investment is about 340 million US dollars.
The 22nd Meeting of the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee on Video was chaired by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Masahiro MIKAMI, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia. In the afternoon of August 30, 2021 at the office of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
This bilateral meeting is part of the Investment Maintenance Mechanism, which has been established since 2009 under the framework of the Agreement between Cambodia and Japan on Liberalization, Promotion and Protection of Investment, signed by Samdech Techo PM. And former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe on June 14, 2007.
During the 22nd meeting, the two sides continued to discuss a number of priority agendas, including: 1: Minimum wage and seniority pay, 2: Tax obligations, 3: Logistics, 4: Supply and price Electricity, 5: Imports of vehicles, 6: Cooperation projects in human resource development, and 7: Organizing workshops to understand how to use the database on (supply chain integration).
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea expressed his deep gratitude to the Japanese investors who have always given high confidence to the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister to ensure peace and political stability, which is necessary for Create a conducive investment environment.
On this occasion, the Minister also thanked the Government and people of Japan for providing medical equipment, ambulances and 1 million doses of AstraZeneca vaccine to Cambodia to prevent the spread of Kovid-19. .
He also expressed hope that ANA would resume direct flights between Japan and Cambodia in the near future, which would help boost trade and investment between the two countries. .
Mr. Masahiro Mikami praised and appreciated the prompt, timely and effective action of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the direct leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 in the Cambodian community. It is the second most populous country in ASEAN to be vaccinated, and as a result the epidemic situation is under control.
In addition, he expressed his appreciation and gratitude to the Council for the Development of Cambodia and relevant ministries and institutions for their past efforts with a high sense of responsibility to facilitate and provide a gentle response to Challenges and requests of Japanese investors, which shows the high attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia to maintain and provide comfort to all investors.
