A woman in Preah Sihanouk province was tried by the court until the Supreme Court ruled to occupy a piece of land, but during the practice, two defendants came out and blocked the couple
The entire land size of 5377 square meters in Sangkat 2, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province has been completely returned to its original owner by the Supreme Court in accordance with the Supreme Court Judgment dated October 12, 2020. In addition, on December 31, 2020, the Supreme Court issued another ruling dismissing a petition for a retrial after the defendant was dissatisfied with the Supreme Court's decision.
Ms. Khov Poseang stated that Mr. Lim Huy Leng and his wife had arbitrarily filed a title deed on her land, and that she had filed a complaint with the Sihanoukville Provincial Court to claim the land. The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court also decided to require Mr. Lim Huy Leng and his wife to return the land to her, citing her land title deed (18010 202.0389) dated April 29, 2015.
The decision of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court was appealed by Mr. Lim Huy Leng and his wife to the Court of Appeal and the Court of Appeal continued to dismiss. The defendant continued to appeal to the Supreme Court, where the Supreme Court still ordered Mr. Lim Huy Leng and his wife, Ung Thavy, to return 5377 square meters of land to Ms. Khov Poseang.
On this issue, Mr. Huy Leng acknowledged that he had indeed lost the case and that he did not oppose the Supreme Court's ruling. But he still claims to be the owner of the land and even acts as a deterrent when the landowner begins to enjoy it.
