Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Thai TV Showcases Cambodia's Investment and Tourism Potential
(Bangkok, Thailand): Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, appeared on Thai television to showcase the investment and tourism potential in Cambodia.
In that interview, Dr. highlighted the complete peace of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which has made Cambodia develop rapidly in all areas on an equal footing with other countries in the region and on the stage. International.
Dr. also emphasized the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to build a strong welfare for the people and foreigners in Cambodia by achieving great success in preventing Kovid-19 through the implementation of measures "3 do not 3 prevent Of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the success of the national vaccination campaign against Kovid-19, which has reached more than 90% of the target population of 10 million people and is continuing to give the third dose (boost dose) to the people.
Mr. Sok Sokretya also informed the audience and Thai investors to understand the new investment law of Cambodia, which is an excellent investment opportunity to find investment opportunities in Cambodia in all areas. In particular, investment in small and medium enterprises (SMEs).
The Prime Minister's personal adviser also informed about the rich tourism potential in Cambodia, international heritage tourism, cultural tourism, historical tourism, ecotourism, eco-tourism, coastal tourism (diving, coral viewing, seabed biodiversity), adventure tourism ( Adventure Tourism) and youth tourism, which is taken care of by the Royal Government of Cambodia to restore and build infrastructure to create new tourism products and facilities to serve the tourism sector.
Taking that opportunity, Dr. also reminded of the good and long-lasting friendship between Cambodia and Thailand will continue to strive to maintain this relationship better and better until the next generation.
