Articles 17 and 18 of the Law on Public Administration (2019) stipulate the rights and obligations that are important for every governor to understand.
The Board of Trustees has the following rights: 1. To receive information related to the management of the Board of Governors, including financial statements, audit reports and other relevant documents, and to appoint and terminate the Board of Directors in accordance with the conditions specified in the letter .
The Board of Trustees has the following duties:
1- Transfer of assets or funds as the principal to the Board of Governors, manage and manage on behalf of the beneficiaries: 2- Participate in or facilitate the transfer of the assets to the Board of Governors to manage and manage. For changes in the administration of donors or contributors to governance or changes in the terms of the governance letter. 4. To comply with the conditions set by the governance letter and the regulations in force.
