Mr. Pan Sosak said that this Memorandum of Understanding is an important event that confirms the cooperation between the Ministry of Commerce and the private sector (Wing Bank) to provide convenience to small and medium enterprises and customers in E-commerce for payment transactions on Cambodia Trade.
Mr. Pan Sosak added that the Ministry of Commerce's Cambodia Trade Market will provide an opportunity for small and medium enterprises to sell potential Cambodian products for domestic sale and export to overseas markets and exhibitions in Cambodia. In a wide and unlimited market that can be called e-commerce to local and international customers.
Han Pengquan also said that the partnership allows Wing to contribute to the development of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia using digital payments. Digital payments are gaining popularity around the world due to their convenience and security.
Wing Bank, widely known for its multi-functional Wing smartphone applications and Wing agents, has nearly 10,000 locations across Cambodia and provides daily financial services. By 2020, Wing Bank was working with more than 2,400 small and medium enterprises, providing collection and payment services.
