BEIJING, Aug. 27 (Xinhua) - The Office of the Director General of the US National Intelligence Agency (NESA) has released a non-confidential assessment report on the 19-year-old Kovid virus surveillance report, saying that intelligence agencies are still unable to comment. The consensus between the "concept of the virus leaked from the laboratory" and the "concept of the virus originating in nature" are the two main views on the origin of the Kovid 19 virus.
In fact, viral and infectious disease experts trace the origin of the Kovid 19 virus as a tedious task. But if an intelligence agency is ordered to track down the source of the Kovid 19 virus, it is very easy because it can only be stored in a charging tube.
Because the United States propagates a false or open statement that China has studied and produced 19 Kovid virus and has spread from China to all over the world, not only can it deny responsibility. And the United States' inability to prevent and control infectious diseases can even invent an ideology for attacking China.
Tracing the origin of the virus as a serious scientific problem requires scientists and medical professionals around the world to work together to conduct research based on facts and evidence and make scientific conclusions.
Science does not allow for the slightest act of fraud, nor does it preclude preconceived notions, nor does it interfere with scientific research through political motives. Ordering intelligence agencies instead of scientists to trace the origin of the Kovid 19 virus violates the scientific and fair red line that makes people completely confused.
Infectious diseases continue to spread, and cooperation in the fight against Kovid 19 is an urgent task today. The United States has deliberately ordered intelligence agencies to track down the source of the 19 19 virus. This act violates scientific principles and lacks public trust. These will add a new stain to America's grim human rights record.
