The following is the press release of the Koh Kong Provincial Administration: TOP NEWS: General Khieu Sopheak: The Ministry of Interior is searching for the person who falsified the information that "Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng met with Mr. Sam Rainsy to form an interim government"
(Phnom Penh): General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, through the official news channel Fresh News on August 29, 2021, confirmed that the Ministry of Interior is searching for the person who falsified the information that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Director General The Minister of Interior met with Sam Rainsy and agreed to form an interim government while Samdech was present in France.
The statement from the spokesman of the Ministry of Interior came after a Facebook account named Tharith Bun posted a picture of the past meeting between Samdech Sar Kheng and Sam Rainsy in the National Assembly in September 2015 and republished it with distorted content. "Samdech has a new meeting with Sam Rainsy in France to form an interim government."
General Khieu Sopheak considers such posting to be an incitement to riots, and now the authorities are searching for the perpetrators and those who distributed the distorted information to cause the riots to take legal action. He urged the public not to pay attention and not to share this provocative information so as not to confuse.
It should be noted that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on August 22, 2021, paid a two-week visit to France due to personal reasons. After being informed of Sar Kheng's private journey, the illegal opposition through the media close to them immediately announced that they would welcome any informal meeting to find a political solution for Sar Kheng. They.
Immediately, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, refused and confirmed that Samdech went to France because he had his own business and no other program.
