Spokesperson: At present, there is about 100 tons of garbage per day in Chattalysak and 19 Kovid Care Centers nationwide.
(Kampot): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, said that according to the report provided by the 25 provincial-capital environment departments, the solid waste generated at Chattalysak and Kovid 19 treatment centers has About 100 tons per day at present, but this number may decrease due to the decline in the rate of Kovid 19 infection.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this statement on the morning of August 28, 2021, during which he and Mr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province and relevant officials inspected the construction site of a solid waste incinerator in Damnak Chang Er Village, Sangkat Prey Thom, Kep City.
Fifty solid waste incinerators equipped by the Ministry of Environment to 21 capitals and provinces (49 districts) have been participating in incineration of medical waste from 19 Kovid Medical Centers and Chandeliers, in addition to existing medical incinerators. In hospitals and health centers throughout Cambodia. This is an additional statement by Mr. Net Pheaktra.
The senior official said that the management and packaging of solid waste from Chattalysak Center and Kovid 19 Hospital and from home care patients, including the spraying of antiseptic, will help prevent the spread of the disease. Outbreaks of Kovid 19.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that in some provinces such as Siem Reap, Mondulkiri, Battambang, etc., high-tech solid waste incinerators are used to incinerate medical waste from Kovid 19 Hospital and Chattalysak Center.
According to Mr. Net Pheaktra, the Ministry of Environment, through the Department of Environment, has provided technical support for the management of solid waste from the Kovid 19 Hospital. To date, the Ministry of Environment has equipped 50 solid waste incinerators to 21 capitals and provinces (49 districts).
At the same time, a spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that the installation of solid waste incinerators is an urgent step forward, and the management of solid waste in a technical manner with the right bins, adequate means of transporting garbage and landfills. Technical scale is a strategic measure of urban solid waste management policy.
"The Ministry of Environment continues to support and strengthen the capacity of sub-national administrations to increase the efficiency of solid waste management." "Cambodia produces more than 10,000 tons of garbage per day, and about 4 million tons per year, of which about 68% is organic waste, more than 20% is plastic waste and more than 10% is solid / hazardous waste." This is the emphasis of Mr. Net Pheaktra.
In addition, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the Ministry of Environment has provided technical training to local officials by: 1) Enabling sub-national administrations to take ownership of solid waste management at the local level. 2) Strengthen the capacity of sub-national administration to manage solid waste at the local level with high efficiency. 3) Improve the quality of the environment to participate in sustainable economic and social development.
According to Mr. Som Piseth, he thanked the Ministry of Environment, especially Minister Say Sam Al, for paying close attention to the management of urban solid waste and providing technical support as well as providing facilities for the provincial administration. Successfully implemented urban solid waste management.
The provincial governor expressed his pride that Kep province has received attention and received the ASEAN Environmental Award.
Mr. Som Piseth said that the solid waste incinerator, which will be put into operation in the next two weeks, will be used to incinerate various waste from the incubator and Kovid 19 patient treatment center, especially medical. Burn in this kiln to effectively control this hazardous waste. At the same time, Mr. Som Piseth continued that the proper packaging of garbage brings a clean environment, fresh air and good health.
While praising the Kep Provincial Administration, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment said that the Ministry of Environment would like to call on the people to participate in packing garbage properly and sorting garbage according to the type, especially to properly pack waste from the treatment center to avoid Throw away trash, which is detrimental to aesthetics and comfort. "Our village, commune, community is clean, we all need to participate," he said.
It should be noted that in order to properly manage the waste and prevent infection, the Capital Administration has advised patients to put garbage in yellow bags or write the label on the bags and separate from other people's garbage for easy collection. .
The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration continued to spray 19 Kovid on the fingers inside and outside the bag and leave the rubbish aside for about five days before releasing it. The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has asked residents to use 15 kg bags to hold the amount of garbage for at least 5 days to avoid discharging it for daily use.
The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has warned that in case of non-cooperation and non-compliance with the above guidelines and causing the transmission of Kovid 19 to others, the perpetrators shall be liable under Article 9 of the Law on Measures to Prevent the Spread of the Disease. Kovid 19.
