(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, donated 5 million Riels through the Governor of Por Senchey District, Mr. Hem Darith, to attend the funeral of a boy who was killed by a murderer in a bathroom of a rented house two days ago. Trapeang Krasaing Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Hem Darith assigned a representative to bring the 5 million Riels to the family of the body to the crematorium in Wat Snor, at the foot of Snor Mountain, Ta Nuon Village, Preah Phos Commune, Koas Kratb District, Battambang Province on the afternoon of the 28th. August 2021 to mourn with the family of the deceased.
According to Mr. Hem Darith's representative, he told Fresh News that it is very sad that the family is very poor. The mother is a widow living in a hut in a remote area and took her son to Phnom Penh to work as a factory worker.
Sources said that on the morning of the incident, the mother went to work in the factory, leaving her son in a rented room alone. In the evening of the same day, after returning from work to the rented room, he could not find his son, so he went to look and found a bag in the bathroom.
The source added that the mother immediately opened the bag and found the body of her son, who was the killer, and lost a 2-gram platinum necklace that her son was wearing and the money she had saved. In ground piglets as well. Later, the woman reported to the authorities to inspect and autopsy to search and arrest the perpetrators to deal with the law.
