(Phnom Penh): Most people think that "owls" can turn their heads 360 degrees, but some opinions do not agree with this view until a new study by scientists and also showed New evidence and arguments to shed light on this skepticism and uncertainty.
What people see as being able to turn their head 360 degrees may be due to confusion through the naked eye. The scientists explained that the owl was able to do this because of its special backbone and muscles, as well as its 14-wheeled skeleton, which was specially designed to allow the bones to move freely. Also, because the wings are bigger on both sides and its thick feathers help to deceive our eyes.
The owl's eyes are round so that the lens of the eye is larger. Their eyes can detect light up to 100 times faster than our human eyes. They can see mice on the ground from a height of 45 meters, even in dim light, the size of a candle.
