(Preah Vihear): On August 28, 2021, this is the third day of the humanitarian mission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to grandparents who are 100 years old or older after volunteering to be vaccinated against Kovid. 19. Today's mission is for four grandmothers in Preah Vihear province to receive gifts from Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's donation was handed over to their back home by Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the Committee for Kovid 19 Vaccination. The road is difficult, however.
The four grandmothers who received gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen include:
In today's mission, the team led by Mrs. O Vandin had to travel for many hours to reach the house of the four grandmothers, and to cross the difficult and narrow road up and down the mountain. And so on. But these are not the obstacles of O Vandin's team.
Remarkably, on that occasion, Ms. O Vandin always brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to visit the four grandmothers and inform them about their health status after vaccination. Also prevent Kovid 19 and why they should be vaccinated.
The four vaccinated women thanked the Prime Minister for allowing him to be vaccinated and given him gifts on this occasion, as their health condition after receiving The Kovid 19 vaccine is in good condition.
They also claimed that the reason they volunteered to be vaccinated was because they feared the 19 cases of Kovid, which are now spreading, especially to new mutants.
