Singapore military plane helps transport 149 Afghan refugees from Qatar to Germany
SINGAPORE, Aug. 28 (Xinhua) - A military transport aircraft has helped transport a total of 149 refugees from Afghanistan to Germany safely, the Ministry of Defense announced on Saturday evening. According to a release by CNA.
According to a statement from the Singapore Ministry of Defense, its military aircraft took the 149 Afghan refugees from Qatar and proceeded to Germany. Qatar and a number of other countries are considered midway destinations for refugees from Afghanistan waiting to travel to third countries.
According to the ministry, Singaporean military planes left the country on Thursday night for Qatar to assist the United States in evacuating Afghans. Singapore has volunteered to help the United States transport refugees from Afghanistan who are temporarily staying in Qatar to a third country as planned.
