(Siem Reap): The Disability Foundation donated a house and some other gifts to a poor disabled person named Son Sotith Vicheka, living in Kantraing village, Kantraing commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province.
The handover ceremony took place on August 28, 2021, with the participation of Mr. Sim Sothoun, Director of the Disability Fund, Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and many other local authorities.
Mr. Sim Sothoun, Director of the Disability Fund, said that according to the report of the Committee for Monitoring and Evaluation of Housing for the Disabled in the Community, the family of the above disabled person has 3 members whose husband is also disabled. In the past, they lived in a dilapidated hut 3 meters by 4 meters and had a low income and was helpless.
Through this report, the Disability Foundation also decided to provide a house of 4 meters by 6 meters made of galvanized stone to his family to improve their well-being and dignity.
The director of the Foundation for the Disabled praised the families of the disabled who have improved their residential land to grow vegetables and raise small frogs to improve their livelihoods.
In addition to this house, the disabled person also received a gift package from the Disability Foundation, including 25 kg of rice, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 2 kg of salt, 2 sticks of fish, 1 box of noodles and 100,000 Riels.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Donates Medical Equipment to Koh Thom District Referral Hospital and Koh Thom District Health Center
(Kandal): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Chairman of the National Working Group of the Royal Government of Koh Thom District, this morning, August 28, 2021, led a team to hand over some medical equipment received from donors to Koh Thom District Referral Hospital and Koh Thom District Health Centers at Koh Thom District Hospital, Kandal Province.
Speaking at the handing over ceremony of medical equipment, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also mentioned the new building structure of Koh Thom District Referral Hospital, which is scheduled to open in October 2021, on the old site. Construction is scheduled for 12 months and is scheduled for completion by the end of 2022.
The new building of this new referral hospital is designed to provide health care and treatment services to patients more efficiently, appropriately, good quality and fast to the people living in Koh Thom district, as well as the people living in the district and nearby areas. Koh Thom district to gain more confidence and warmth in receiving health services from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also informed that the hospital has 150 beds, a third-class hospital equipped with adequate medical equipment under the support and close cooperation of Calmette Hospital.
