Doctors of the 5th Military Region continue to vaccinate 19 people in Preah Net Preah district
(Banteay Meanchey): A group of doctors from the 5th Army Division, in their mobile vehicles, this morning, Saturday, August 28, 2021, launched a campaign to vaccinate 19 people in Covey Vary commune, Preah Net Preah district, province. Banteay Meanchey.
The vaccination campaign for the people in Preah Net Preah district was led by Major General Chhun Mao, Deputy Commander of the 5th Military Zone, Deputy Commander of the 1st Division, Banteay Meanchey, and Brigadier General Sing Tum, Commander of the 51st New Brigade.
About 30,000 people in Preah Net Preah district were vaccinated against Kovid 19. The team plans to spend about 20 days vaccinating the first dose for the people and then giving the second dose to them.
During the vaccination campaign for the people of Preah Net Preah district this morning, Brigadier General Sing Tum instructed the people who came to receive the first dose to follow the doctor's instructions and continue to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health. In particular, continue to implement the "3 Do 3 Protect" measures of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19.
Kovid 19 vaccine is an essential method of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect people from the Kovid 19 outbreak. Banteay Meanchey, a province bordering Thailand, is also being taken care of by the Royal Government and vaccinated.
The border province was vaccinated by Army medics from the 5th Army Division. According to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the guidance of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, as well as the Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Ou Rath, the Army Medical Team of the 5th Military Zone paid high attention to Vaccination work for this people.
Doctors have also set up vehicles to mobilize people in remote areas to vaccinate.
People who have been vaccinated have been overjoyed and excited. They thanked the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for seeking to vaccinate them to prevent Kovid-19.
The people also thanked the doctors, the army and all the relevant authorities who took great care to vaccinate them.
