Britain claims to close evacuation operation from Afghanistan on Saturday
LONDON (Reuters) - The British military has announced that its evacuation operation from Kabul, Afghanistan, will end on Saturday, August 28, 2021. According to a release by the BBC.
British military and civilian aircraft have joined the United States and other countries in evacuating people from Afghanistan since the Taliban took control of Kabul. From August 13 to 27, Britain evacuated a total of 14,543 people from Afghanistan.
According to the British military commander, the evacuation by the British will end on Saturday, but it is not clear how many more people will be able to be evacuated from Afghanistan. On Friday, the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Boris Johnson, said he would do his best to help Afghans eligible for resettlement in the United Kingdom leave the city. Kabul.
However, the decision of the British military on Saturday came after Kabul airport was hit by a suicide bombing that killed 182 people, 13 of them US troops, while the United States. He warned that there could be more attacks by ISIS-K in Afghanistan. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit donated 5 tons of lentils to Prey Veng Provincial Administration.
