Ministry of Tourism signed a memorandum of understanding with Cambodian entrepreneurs to help people in the tourism community to create and expand businesses other than tourism services
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Cambodian Entrepreneurs on the project "Promoting Internal Tourism Movement and Promoting Tourism Activities in Tourism Communities in the Context of the Kovid-19 Crisis" to help communities in each tourism community Create new business on your own and expand your business in addition to tourism services.
The signing ceremony was held between Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of the General Department of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, Ministry of Tourism, and Mr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Khmer Entrepreneurship, under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on 27 August. 2021.
In an interview with reporters, Mr. Thong Rathsak said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding is a very important work in cooperation to promote the internal tourism movement before the opening of international tourists. In the future, while the campaign to vaccinate people across the country is also going smoothly, especially the third dose or boost dose.
The Director General stated that in this first step, the Ministry of Tourism and Cambodian entrepreneurs have agreed to select five tourism communities to help develop and train according to standards and financial resources, with the five communities in four provinces, including :
Siem Reap Province: Teuk Chob Khnar Po Ecotourism Community in Sotnikum District and Changkarn Roi Tourism Community in Varin District.
* Battambang Province: O'Choam Waterfall Tourism Community in Samlot District.
Pursat Province: Reang Khvav Tourism Community, Kravanh District.
* Kampong Chhnang Province: Sre Ampil Tourism Community in Teuk Phos District.
He said that the Ministry of Tourism will contribute to the development of those communities by focusing on training on the implementation of tourism safety rules, health rules in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis and post-crisis. In addition, there are training on food standards, farm trips for local and international guests, and other face-to-face training.
Cambodian entrepreneurs also have financial resources to help directly to the community and to provide technical training, business creation, business expansion and business to the community, especially Cambodian entrepreneurs have many other development partners to help. .
Mr. Chheang Vann Monin said that seeing that the Ministry of Tourism has clear standards in community development, tourism training standards, that's why Cambodian entrepreneurs want to participate in community development with the Ministry of Tourism to increase the attractiveness of tourists from all walks of life. Visit in those tourism communities to help the community earn a better income.
Mr. Chheang Vann Monin said, "The community is not only welcoming, but the community can expand its business and have the ability to receive a high level of tourists and can attract investment." If there is a system of income and expenditure management system, there is clear accountability, there is a good business model, Cambodian entrepreneurs will have the courage to continue to help prepare their business model more.
According to Mr. Vann Monin, Cambodian entrepreneurs really want to help those five communities become a model community in Cambodia so that other tourism communities can follow their example so that their communities can continue to grow.
The Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurs added that the community has the opportunity to attract businessmen or investors both in the country and abroad to continue to develop their communities, and investors are happy to invest in those communities. He said that if the banking sector wants to invest in the development of tourism communities, it would be even better. These are opportunities and incentives for each tourism community.
Mr. Chheang Vann Monin also said that the financial resources that Cambodian entrepreneurs have for use are 100% loans from the Ministry of Economy and Finance under the consideration of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Chairman of the Management and Development Committee. Tourism.
In addition, Director-General Thong Rathsak revealed that when those communities are well developed, they will be able to expand the scope of international tourists to enter those communities, but must comply with the standards. In particular, tourism safety rules, health rules and so on.
He added that through this first step, the Ministry of Tourism also wants the five communities, as well as other communities in Cambodia, to receive the ASEAN Model Community Award in the upcoming ASEAN Tourism Forum 2023. Up in Indonesia.
Please be informed that before the signing of the above memorandum, Minister Thong Khon also fully encouraged this cooperation because it is in line with the "Roadmap on the plan to restore and promote tourism in Cambodia and After the Kovid-19 crisis, which has already been approved by the Royal Government.
