Thailand to lift most restrictions from September, especially in Bangkok, to revive the economy
The easing of austerity measures is needed to revive the national economy as the country fights its worst pandemic and is trying to increase vaccination rates.
From September 1, supermarkets, barbershops, massage parlors and gyms in 29 high-risk provinces, including Bangkok, will be allowed to reopen. Open reception as usual.
In this regard, the Thai authorities have asked business operators to ensure that their service personnel receive a complete vaccination (2 doses) and regularly tested and required customers to show proof of vaccination and testing. Negative for the disease as well.
