General Knowledge: The 5 Largest Giant Lakes in the World
Here are the five largest lakes in the world, all of which are naturally occurring:
First place: Caspian Sea The Caspian Sea covers an area of 371,000 square kilometers and has a maximum depth of 1,025 meters below sea level. The Caspian Sea is considered to be one of the dividing points between Europe and Asia, with countries bordering the sea including Kazakhstan, Russia, Turkmenistan, Azerbaijan and Iran.
Despite its name as the sea, the Caspian is now considered the largest lake on earth because it is apparently not connected to the oceans. It is called such a sea because in history since ancient times it has been considered a sea. The name Caspian is derived from a group of white tribes who lived near the area.
