For almost 8 months in 2021, professional officers found 197 stations and depots selling dishonest business
(Phnom Penh): In the first eight months of 2021, the General Department of KPR inspected 447 fuel stations and depots, including those that did not comply with the business. To 197 consumer protection laws.
Of these, 184 depots were investigated by the Investigative Officer of the General Department of KPR, who was rehabilitated as judicial police, implemented transitional penalties according to the type of crime, and 13 depots were warned in writing and contracted to stop This unrighteous act continues.
According to the content of the Law on Consumer Protection, in the event of a one-time transaction penalty and then continuing to commit an offense, the business registration or license will be suspended, revoked or revoked.
In case the perpetrator refuses to pay the transaction fine, the investigating officer shall build a case of the offense and send it to the competent court. In 2021, no station or depot owner has yet been sent to court by the Investigating Officer of the General Department of KPR.
The General Department of KPR will continue to inspect fuel stations and depots throughout the country and implement the strictest legal measures to strictly prevent dishonest business related to fuel to protect the interests of the people. As a user.
