The following is the press release of Pailin Provincial Administration: Capital Gain Tax will be implemented on January 1, 2022
(Phnom Penh): If nothing changes, the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance will start collecting tax revenue on capital gains tax from January 1, 2022 after this tax is postponed. Practice for one year.
Speaking on the program "Tax of Cambodia" on "Tax on Capital Gains" on August 26, 2021, Mr. Chey Rithy, Deputy Director of the Department of Property and Real Estate Tax of the General Department of Taxation said that the tax on capital gains will be applied at Early next year on January 1, 2022.
He said that the General Department of Taxation has been preparing more draft guidelines to facilitate taxpayers in implementing the tax obligations on capital gains as well.
Resident legal entities who have already registered the tax and declared the annual income tax are no longer liable for this tax. Capital gains tax is levied on capital gains achieved at the time of the sale or transfer of profitable capital only, in the absence of profit, there is no obligation to pay this tax.
For the calculation of tax on capital gain is the profit from the sale or transfer of capital multiplied by the tax rate of 20%, and for capital as real estate, the property owner can choose the method of deducting expenses. Expenditures account for 80% of the proceeds from the sale or transfer of real estate;
