White House: 19,000 evacuated from Afghanistan in last 24 hours
The Pentagon said Tuesday that more than 5,000 people were waiting for boarding at Kabul Airport, which now leaves every 45 minutes.
In addition, two U.S. defense officials told CNN that the first U.S. troops had begun leaving the country as the evacuation mission entered its final week.
US President Joe Biden has vowed not to delay the withdrawal of all US troops from Afghanistan by the 31st of August, despite pressure from all directions. Ask him to extend the time for the evacuation operation.
However, Biden said the delay in the evacuation operation was due to concerns about a terrorist attack on Kabul airport by ISIS in Afghanistan, also known as ISIS-K.
