Police arrest two thieves for stealing motorcycles of military officers
(Phnom Penh): Kambol District Criminal Police and Kambol Police arrested two suspects for stealing a motorcycle while its owner was parked in front of a rented room and confiscated the motorcycle along with the license plate. Multi-plate motorcycle numbers and some motorcycle parts as well.
This incident happened at 12:30 pm on August 23, 2021 at a rented house in Kampoul village, Kampoul commune, Kampoul district, Phnom Penh.
Police said that before the incident, the victim left a Honda Dream 125 motorcycle in front of the rented room. After locking up, the victim went to sleep inside the room.
At the time of the incident, the two suspects went to steal a motorcycle and escaped, but the owner of the motorcycle woke up and shouted "thieves", causing a surprise to the police force. Kambol district criminal police and Kambol administrative police station are patrolling the road, and they helped chase and arrest one suspect and one of them escaped.
After the arrest, the force took him to be interrogated until August 24. Mr. Chhim Savuth, Deputy Inspector in charge of Criminal Planning, Kambol District, led the force to arrest another member of the gang, confiscating two motorcycles and 5 motorcycle license plates. Some other motorcycle parts.
