A spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources highlights the high efficiency of the drainage system in Sihanoukville, two years ago it rained for nearly 300 millimeters, it took 72 hours to recover, but last night it rained for only 90 minutes, the water completely receded
Mr. Chan Yutha, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, considered that the comparison of the above-mentioned floods in Sihanoukville reflected the excellent efficiency of the Royal Government in its efforts to organize and organize water release infrastructure. In this province in the past.
However, the senior official expressed his condolences for the impact on housing, property, and the loss of one person due to this natural disaster. Once prepared, the impact will be even greater.
Comparison points:
* 2019: Rainfall over a longer period of time than flooding (then heavy flooding in Sangkat 3 and Sangkat 4). After 36 hours of dry weather, the floodwaters began to recede in Sangkat 3, and after about 72 hours, the flood situation eased.
* 2021: Shorter rainfall but more rainfall. The flooding was only in Sangkat 4, and Sangkat 3 was not flooded. Interestingly, after about 90 minutes of rain, the floodwaters receded. This is the additional confirmation of this spokesperson.
Through the above comparison, Mr. Chan Yutha concluded and highlighted the effectiveness of the Royal Government, which has tried to organize the drainage infrastructure in Sihanoukville in the past.
