Siem Reap City Administration decides to transfer Kovid-19 vaccination site from Siem Reap Health Center to Wat Bo Primary School
(Siem Reap): On August 24, 2021, the Siem Reap Municipal Administration, in cooperation with the Sala Kamroeuk Sangkat Administration, met with the Director of the Siem Reap Operational Health Office and decided to transfer the Kovid-19 vaccination site from Siem Reap Health Center to Wat Bo Primary School.
According to the Siem Reap Municipal Administration, this work is to facilitate and avoid waiting in the sun during the waiting period to vaccinate children and grandchildren from 12 years old. Under 18 years old, because the previous location did not have a proper roof, prone to sunburn.
Wat Bo Primary School has a roof and a large yard suitable for waiting for the Kovid 19 vaccination shift, and the transfer of the Kovid 19 vaccination site from August 25 to September 1.
The authorities also ask the guardians living in Slor Kram and Sala Kamroeuk communes to be informed and to keep the distance between them properly while waiting for the vaccination shift.
