(Phnom Penh): Under the guidance and guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh has cooperated with the Department of Water Resources and local authorities to rehabilitate several main canals in Phnom Penh and confirmed that These rehabilitation will be completed by the end of August to relieve the flooding of people's villages.
The canals that the team has already implemented and are currently carrying out rehabilitation work include:
* Main Toul Pong 1 Canal, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey, size 8 meters and depth 2 meters, built 7 bridges and bumped along the mouth of the main canal to prevent landslides. . This canal plays an important role in draining the flood water from National Road 3 in Meanchey district to Choeung Ek Lake and continues to flow into the deep river.
* Main Toul Pong II Canal is located in Sangkat Choam Chao 2 and Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey to drain rainwater and sewage from National Road 3 to Prek Ha Canal.
* Melu 5 Canal is a canal that is recognized as an important canal for local water release in Khan Por Senchey, Khan Sen Sok and Khan Meanchey. And.
* Stung Meanchey main canal, the team has been building by pouring concrete, the wall of the canal is more than 1,500 meters long, although it is not finished yet, but this canal can drain water well without any problem.
Memel Canal in Phoum Mol, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, 2,815 meters long, 20 to 30 meters wide, from the 5th drainage pumping station to the Boeung Tompun pumping station, is scheduled to be completed by the end of August 2021.
* Two main canals on either side of the railway from National Road 4 connected to O'Lao Canal, the team has restored to open the water to flow to the Kob Srov Dam Lake. This canal plays an important role in relieving flooding in the western part of Phnom Penh, especially in the territory of the whole Kambol district and part of Por Sen Chey district.
Rehabilitation of the main canal of Boeung Tumpun, which is 3,710 meters long and 30 meters wide from Stung Meanchey canal to Boeung Tumpun station on Street 371. This canal plays an important role in releasing water from Doeum Sleng canal, French canal, especially liberating water from Khan Por Senchey, Khan Sen Sok, Khan Toul Kork and some parts in Khan Chamkarmon and Khan 7 Makara.
Rehabilitation of Prek O Khsach, which is 16,799 meters long, 26 meters high, 17 meters deep and 3 meters deep, located in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, 2,049 meters long and 14,750 meters long in Phnom Penh. This canal is responsible for releasing water from Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province, then Sangkat Kambol, Sangkat Ovulok, Sangkat Snor, Khan Kambol and continues to flow into Boeung Ta Mok.
Rehabilitation of the main Boeung Ha canal, which is more than 2 km long, from the stone bridge on Prey Sar Road to the Lumpram pumping station in Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
