BEIJING (Reuters) - China is now the world's largest trading nation and the world's second-largest consumer market, the Ministry of Commerce recently announced. By 2020, China's total retail sales of consumer goods will reach 39.2 trillion yuan. Consumption will be the first driving force of China's economic growth for several consecutive years.
According to the announcement, it is not difficult to see that the Chinese market, with a population of up to 1.4 billion, has huge consumption potential, which is very popular with the country's traders and investors. The world has become one of the largest investment and trade destinations.
Under the policy of reform and opening up, China has increasingly opened its doors to all friendly countries and traded on freedom, honesty, justice, equality and win-win. Therefore, we see that almost all countries in the world have good trade relations with China and benefit from each other, more or less.
As we have already seen, many free trade agreements have been signed by China with partner countries and regions, especially the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which is a free trade area. The world's largest is expected to deliver enormous economic benefits, as well as deepen the partnership of signatory countries to bring benefits and happiness to the people of the region as well as the world.
As the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen once stressed, "China has played an important role in the current global economic, trade and political activities, and China's assistance not only contributes to development and "Let Cambodia not only lift itself out of poverty, but also help strengthen Cambodia's independence."
What should be more expected of the people of Cambodia and China, as well as traders and investors of the two countries is the signing of the upcoming Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which will greatly contribute to Rehabilitate and develop the bilateral economy as well as restore people's livelihood to normal after the end of Kovid-19 to bring greater benefits to investors and people of both countries.
