(Phnom Penh): Before concluding his position, Mr. Pehin Dato Abdul Ramanthip, President of the 42nd AIPA General Assembly and Chairman of the Legislative Council of Brunei Darussalam, handed over the 43rd position of President of AIPA to Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President National Assembly of Cambodia.
The 42nd Annual Meeting of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA), hosted by the Brunei Darussalam Parliament, closed successfully on the afternoon of August 25, 2021, after three days.
As the 42nd General Assembly was held on video, the transfer of the IPA to Samdech Heng Samrin took place through the Cambodian Ambassador to Brunei Darussalam. Abdul Ramantip.
Mr. Pehin Dato Abdul Ramantip, as well as all IPA members, are extremely pleased with the transfer of the IPA President to the Cambodian Parliament and firmly believe that under the leadership of Samdech Heng Samrin, the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly in 2022 will be a great achievement in promoting parliamentary mechanisms and promoting solidarity cooperation between ASEAN and IPA to effectively address the challenges of the people of the region and the world.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin congratulates the Legislative Council of Brunei Darussalam for successfully hosting the 42nd IPA General Assembly on video during the Kovid-19 pandemic. On behalf of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, I would like to accept the responsibility of the President of the IPA from Mr. Pehin Dato Abdul Ramantip, President of the Legislative Council of Brunei Darussalam.
As the 43rd President of IPA, Samdech Heng Samrin emphasized that the Cambodian Parliament looks forward to working closely with the IPA Secretariat, as well as the IPA Member Parliament and its partner countries to continue to strengthen our good work and ensure the achievement of the IPA. ASEAN's shared vision and aspirations, in particular the achievement of a people-centered and people-centered ASEAN community.
Please be reminded that the 42nd General Assembly, hosted by the Parliament of Brunei Darussalam this year, under the theme "Promoting Parliamentary Cooperation in the Digital Environment towards the ASEAN Community 2025". Svay Rieng Provincial Administration Identifies 5 Kovid Patients, Nine Cured
