Mr. Hermin Khem: This is the most difficult time of business in the context of Kovid-19, which we launched in early January. And this is our difficult task, we have to learn how to get through this storm and prepare various plans and special offers for customers.
3: Hyatt Regency Hotel Phnom Penh, which has a program "Take care of your well-being" and implement strict hygiene measures to adapt to the current context. Can you confirm how the program is implemented?
Mr. Hermin Khem: The focus on hygiene and well-being has been practiced with Hai Yat for a long time and has become one of our most important principles. During the Kovid-19 eruption, this is a time when we must continue to apply and adhere to our principles more thoroughly. Taking care of well-being is the most important part of life for our colleagues and for our general guests.
We must make sure that we practice and pay the utmost attention to hygiene and well-being throughout our entire hotel complex. Due to the thorough and dedicated implementation of the Sanitation and Wellness Measures, we are accredited and have received the standard quality certification by GBAC Star on Hygiene and Welfare Care.
4: Is the implementation of the strict hygiene measures of the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel implemented in accordance with the hygiene measures or in accordance with any international standards?
Mr. Hermin Khem: For one of the standards that we have been applying to the hygiene and welfare measures in the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel, it is in accordance with the high hygiene standards of GBAC Star. This is a program that Hyatt Hotels around the world are implementing to help prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus.
This is a recognition that focuses on hygiene standards to ensure that our guests and colleagues have high confidence in hygiene standards and safety. We are recognized by international institutions for implementing this hygiene standard. For this program, we are reviewed annually by the US-based Sanitation Standards Inspection Agency, ensuring that all measures are followed consistently.
Our hygiene protocols and standards include: We regularly disinfect all premises inside and outside the hotel, frequently inspecting and disinfecting the rooms for guests before and after the stay of all colleagues and guests entering the hotel premises. Adhere to the principle of wearing a mask, washing hands and measuring temperature.
5: How does the Hyatt Regency Hotel Phnom Penh contribute to the revitalization of the hotel and tourism industry?
We will do everything we can to let guests know that in Cambodia it is safe to do business here, safe to travel to Cambodia and safe to travel in Cambodia. And we hope that in November and next year we will see an improvement in business and tourism in Cambodia.
6: Next year, he expects the recovery of tourism. Can you clarify a little bit, what are the foundations that support the expectation of improving the tourism sector next year?
Mr. Hermin Khem: I can raise some arguments. As we have now seen, the vaccination campaign is working well, we see that management in Cambodia is very good. And at that time, Cambodia may have to decide when we can open the border for international travelers, when we can return to normal in a new way. We can look at ASEAN countries with high confidence that the situation will improve next year.
We have received some inquiries from tour companies for the end of this year and the beginning of next year. In addition, we have interested visitors coming to our hotel for business inquiries meetings, which gives us confidence in the return of international tourism later this year and this year. Next.
7. The Royal Government of Cambodia has a nationwide campaign to accelerate immunization and is reaching out to vaccinate children. Can you clarify a bit how this campaign will help boost the recovery of tourism and business in Cambodia.
If the situation returns as expected, some neighboring countries will start coming to Cambodia, which could improve tourism, hospitality, restaurants and trade in the future. This.
