The High Representative of the Prime Minister, Dr. Sok Sokretya, requested the Minister of Labor as well as the Thai authorities to address the plight of Cambodian workers during the Kovid 19 epidemic and to help them receive treatment when they become infected. Kovid 19 and so on.
In response to this request, the Thai Minister of Labor promised to continue to take care of Cambodian workers by facilitating their livelihoods and developing measures to deal with the many consequences during the Kovid-19 crisis. The Minister also claimed that the Thai side will prepare a special memorandum of understanding between Cambodia and Thailand to repatriate both legal and illegal Cambodian workers to work in Thailand, although the Kovid-19 epidemic has not yet recovered. .
The Thai Minister of Labor has also promised that the Thai government will provide 19 Kovid vaccinations to all Cambodian workers working and living in Thailand without recidivism.
The promise of the Thai Minister of Labor is a new hope to alleviate the plight of Cambodian workers in Thailand today. On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Dr. Sok Sokretya expressed his deep gratitude to the Thai Ministry of Labor, the Thai authorities and the Thai government for their commitment to providing high protection to Cambodian workers.
