Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the Interfaith Program against Human Trafficking and the Kovid 19 Global Epidemic on the evening of August 20, 2021.
For more than a year and a half, Cambodia, as well as other countries in the world, has been plagued by Kovid 19. For Cambodia, from February 20, 2021 to the present, there has been an acute outbreak of Kovid 19 in the community.
To prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia, under Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has put in place a number of health measures to curb the spread of Kovid 19. Prompt identification of patients, isolation of stakeholders or closure of highly contagious areas are essential health measures to eliminate the transmission of Kovid 19.
It is based on these health rules that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has introduced measures to block areas in Phnom Penh, Kandal and other provinces, and has also introduced measures requiring people to be isolated at home. And so on.
The government's move has drawn criticism from human rights activists and anti-government groups. They see the government's measures as suppressing the rights and freedoms of the people.
To date, Cambodia has detected a total of nearly 90,000 Kovid 19 cases. Of those, 1,762 died and nearly three were hospitalized.
The Royal Government of Cambodia is continuing to fight the global epidemic by enforcing health regulations, especially arranging for workers from Thailand to be vaccinated at the border to prevent the spread of the virus into the community.
Through the results that Cambodia has achieved, there is strong support from the World Health Organization and other international development organizations. The international community considers this result to be the achievement of the best anti-Kovid 19 action.
However, in today's ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, continues to call on our compatriots to continue to maintain and implement the principles of prevention and health "3 protection and 3 do not" to be consistent, not neglected and must come together Get vaccinated against Kovid 19, which the government provides for free to everyone to build immunity from this deadly pandemic.
