It should be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on October 26, 2020, announced the opening of the subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout for people to temporarily traffic after the opening of the subway. Residents have been temporarily able to see that the traffic situation from National Road 4 to Russian Federation Road is good.
The subway is a 470-meter-long, 8.5-meter-wide lane from National Road 4 to Russian Federation Boulevard for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
The Choam Chao flyover and subway is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, contracted by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC), with a construction period of 30 months and a construction cost of approximately US $ 22 million.
It should be noted that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout officially opened the construction site on June 29, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany. Hun Sen.
