(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on August 19 issued a press release regarding the case of Banteay Srei Forestry Administration District stopping a postal delivery truck of Virak Bun Tham Company.
In the past two days, information has been shared on social media and in the media about the case of Banteay Srei Forestry Administration, which seized a postal delivery truck of Virak Bun Tham Company on August 17, 2021 to fine According to the Forestry Administration Law, after checking and transporting two cases of dead geckos, 989 animals, weighing 66 kilograms.
In this case, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications is closely monitoring the situation, as Virak Buntham is a company that has received a postal service license issued by the Ministry.
