Therefore, in order to protect human health, the Ministry has presented the following UV index, color, graphic, risk level and guidelines for public health protection:
* Red is a very high UV index of 8 to 10, meaning there is a high risk when exposed to sunlight for a long time. Extra vigilance and extra protection for skin and eyes.
Reduce time in the sun between 10 and 4 p.m. If you are outdoors, seek shade, wear long clothing, gloves, sunscreen, a hat, and UV goggles. Apply SPF 30+ sunscreen every 1.5 hours, even when it is cloudy and after swimming or sweating.
* Purple is a very high UV index of 11 or more, which means it is very dangerous when exposed to sunlight for long periods of time. Be careful of skin and eyes. Avoid sun exposure between 10 and 4 p.m.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology said that the increase in the UV index will pose a risk and affect the health of people, animals and plants, so the public must pay more attention to this phenomenon.
