According to Wang Wintian, from the beginning, China has always adhered to a scientific attitude when participating in global cooperation in tracking up COVID-19 sources based on scientific principles. WHO experts have been invited to China twice to investigate the origin of the virus.
He claimed that in March 2021, the WHO officially released a joint report prepared by the joint WHO-China research team, which provided accurate, professional and scientific conclusions on the detection of viral sources. The majority of opinions in the international scientific community felt that it was almost impossible for COVID-19 to be leaked from the laboratory.
However, the United States has turned the global epidemic crisis into a political one and has tried to discriminate against China by using terms such as "Wuhan virus" and using surveillance as a weapon to attack. China to shift responsibility for its failure to respond to the COVID-19 crisis and to achieve its political goals is to discredit and block other countries. This is what Ambassador Touch emphasized.
The ambassador said that all of these actions have posed a major obstacle to scientific-based efforts to track the source of the virus and to efforts to combat the global epidemic. The US political gamble has been met with strong opposition from the international community.
So far, 76 countries have written to the Director-General of the World Health Organization (WHO), emphasizing that tracking down the source of the virus is a purely scientific issue that should not be turned into a political issue. China and the WHO should have full support.
Politicians, the media, experts and people from many countries have come forward to accuse the United States of trying to turn viral work into politics. More than 20 million Chinese people have also submitted online petitions to the WHO urging an investigation into the Fort Detrick Biological Laboratory in the United States.
