The Ministry of Defense's vaccination process is seen to be in full swing and has led to acclaim. But there are also issues related to the production of vaccines.
The production of vaccines by the Ministry of National Defense is different from the Ministry of Health. It is wrong to say that the injection with the Ministry of Health is to get the vaccination card immediately from the first dose. In particular, vaccinations with the Ministry of Defense do not receive a license immediately.
On Tuesday, August 17, 2021, General Ith Sarath visited the Vaccination Card Production Center in the 70th Brigade and the Ministry of National Defense Health Institute to inspect the vaccination card production process. At the card production site, the team was observed to be in a hurry and pay the utmost attention to the production of the vaccine card.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Vaccination Operations of the Ministry of National Defense, emphasized that the inability to provide immunization licenses immediately due to the production of vaccines at the Ministry of Defense requires clear verification. Especially putting your photo on the card.
According to General Ith Sarath, when vaccinated against Kovid 19, the people have to take photos and relevant documents, send them to the database, then enter the data and print it later.
General Ith Sarath said that according to the plan to produce about 2.7 million vaccines, the team has already produced about 1.2 million and entered 2.2 million data. Separately, the data of the players that have not been entered is about 500,000.
Currently, the Ministry of National Defense has set up a commission to oversee and promote the production of vaccines to speed up the production of vaccines. The vaccination team has nearly 2,000 members.
General Ith Sarath called on people who have been vaccinated with the Ministry of National Defense not to worry about not getting a license, as the team is speeding up the process and the production of the card will be completed soon.
General Ith Sarath appealed, "I would like to inform all our people to know that, in general, do not worry that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has not been given a card, it is not easy to get a card." Please be patient, it will not take long to get a card, please be patient. We work very hard, especially Samdech Pichey Sena, he strives to guide and point out to technicians to find ways to produce up to date.
Regarding this vaccination card, Mr. Ith Sarath called on the people who have received the vaccination card to take good care not to lose it because it is necessary to use it in the future.
Regarding the issuance of licenses, General Ith Sarath said that when the production is completed, the team will hand over to the Gendarmerie to be distributed to the people for Phnom Penh. In the provinces, it is handed over to the provincial military.
In connection with the issuance of the vaccination card, the Ministry team also set up a special technology system, when the card is handed over to the people, there is a message to the phone number of the vaccine for more information. Also.
