Mr. Hun Many: The future of Cambodia must be in the hands of Cambodia itself
(Phnom Penh): At a time when the world is paying attention to the events of the war in Afghanistan, especially the collapse of the US-backed government, Hun Many, a young Cambodian lawmaker, has highlighted his views on choosing a political line. In order for Cambodia to be able to maintain a better future and avoid the crises of the past.
In a message on the Facebook page accompanied by the relics of King Norodom Sihanouk, the relics of the King of Cambodia and the image of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Hun Many stated that ownership of one's own destiny is a definite determining factor. On the future of Cambodia.
The young lawmaker also mentioned the policy of "internal reform, increase external friends in the spirit of independence", a political line set by the Cambodian People's Party. For Mr. Hun Manin, this policy means all angles for every Cambodian to know that the future of Cambodia must be in the hands of Cambodia itself.
Mr. Hun Many also highlighted the CPP's policy of "internal reform, increase external friends in the spirit of independence." He added that this policy means all things to all Cambodians, knowing that the future of Cambodia must be in the hands of Cambodia itself.
"There are many lessons in history, both old and new, that teach us to understand that ownership of one's own destiny is a definite determinant of a country's future, while the extent of friendship is a catalyst for peace," said Hun Many. The owner is stronger in line with his internal efforts. "Going forward, we must work together to implement this policy consistently for the future of our children."
Hun Many's message comes as the Afghan government, backed by the United States, was overthrown by Taliban militants as the United States ceased to be a base. The image of the current fall of the Afghan government also reminds me of the fall of the republic in 1975 after the United States ceased to be a base.
The message highlighted by the young Cambodian MPs is now seen as intended to remind the people not to adopt an attitude of dependence on this or that country, which eventually leads to a crisis or collapse. An example in Afghanistan as well as the Khmer Republic.
The Taliban have ruled Afghanistan for just over six years. On October 7, 2001, the United States, under former President George W. Bush, declared war on the Taliban after refusing to hand over and provide hiding places to al-Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden. Washington has been accused of being behind the September 11, 2001 terrorist attacks.
Abdul Hakim Haqqani is the Taliban's chief negotiator and chair of the influential Council of Religious Affairs. Hakim Hakkani is believed to be one of Akun Zada's most trusted people.
Currently, only four countries support the Taliban, including Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates and Turkmenistan, while the United States and the United Nations, as well as most other countries, are unlikely to recognize the Taliban. But some countries, such as China, seem to be showing a tendency to recognize the Taliban as a legitimate government following a recent meeting between senior Chinese and Taliban diplomats in Beijing.
