According to Dr. Phan Phalla, the government established the Cambodian SME Bank not for the purpose of competing with commercial banks and other private financial institutions, but to help fill gaps in the banking sector by operating with financial institutions. Private sector in order to enable small and medium enterprises to get financing at reasonable interest rates.
The second phase of the $ 100 million SME Support Co-financing Project will provide low-interest loans to boost the development of small and medium-sized enterprises in priority sectors such as industry, services and trade. Imports serve local needs or serve as inputs in the production of large companies.
Funds under this co-financing scheme are a co-financing joint venture between the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia (IUCC) and participating financial institutions. There are 26 participating financial institutions in this co-financing project, including 21 commercial banks, 1 specialized bank, 3 deposit-taking microfinance institutions, and 1 microfinance institution.
