The following is a decision by the Ministry of Justice: The President of Indonesia explains the management of the Kovid-19 situation, which requires a balance between public health and the economy.
In his annual address to the Indonesian people ahead of the 76th Independence Day celebrations on Tuesday, Widodo said the government must continue to make decisions based on data as well as science. And the latest technology as Indonesia continues to fight COVID-19, which has already claimed at least 117,000 lives.
Widodo also stressed that the government's goal is to be coherent, but that the strategy and management of the sector must be dynamic and adapt to the challenges. Restrictions and easing of travel in the community, for example, must be made weekly on the basis of the latest data.
"That is what we need to do to find the best combination of public health and economic benefits, because this vicious virus is constantly evolving," Widodo said. "So the solution has to change according to the challenges we face."
