Read the full announcement of the Ministry of Commerce: The second phase of the $ 100 million SME Support Co-financing Project has been launched
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on August 16, 2021 issued a press release on "Launching the" Phase II Co-financing Project for Supporting Small and Medium Enterprises Phase II "worth $ 100 million. .
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on August 16, 2021, the second phase of the Small and Medium Enterprise Co-financing Project has been established and will be officially launched from now on. Go.
The co-financing project aims to provide low-interest loans to promote the development of small and medium-sized enterprises in priority sectors such as industry, services and trade, in lieu of imports, serving domestic demand or serving as input in the production of Large companies and so on.
The funds under this co-financing project amount to US $ 100 million, which is an equal contribution financing between the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, CCHR and the participating financial institutions.
There are 26 participating financial institutions in this co-financing project, including 21 commercial banks, 1 specialized bank, 3 deposit-taking microfinance institutions, and 1 microfinance institution.
Small and medium enterprises with credit requirements can apply for a loan under this co-financing scheme at any participating financial institution, subject to the terms of the co-financing scheme and the lending conditions of each participating financial institution.
Dr. Phan Phalla, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of the Small and Medium Enterprises Bank of Cambodia (CBME), said that small and medium enterprises play an important role in contributing to economic development. National and job creation.
Dr. Phan Phalla hopes that the second phase of the SME Support Co-financing Project will make a significant contribution to supporting small and medium enterprises in maintaining their business stability in these difficult times and preparing for recovery. After the Kovid-19 crisis.
At the same time, Dr. Phan Phalla confirmed that the second phase of the project with a budget of 100 million dollars, including $ 50 million with the participation of the Royal Government and another $ 50 million with the participation of private financial institutions.
He pointed out that the second phase of the project will improve some of the inactive points and improve the loan conditions for small and medium enterprises by increasing the loan size up to 500,000 USD for small and medium enterprises. An average.
"Cover more businesses, lower interest rates to 6.5% for priority businesses, but raise interest rates to 7.5% for general business and maintain lending for up to seven years. " This is an additional emphasis of Dr. Phan Phalla.
Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that small and medium enterprises are the backbone of the Cambodian economy because they contribute significantly to the country's gross domestic product (GDP) and create jobs. Cambodians too.
Dr. In Channy stated that one of the main challenges is financing, which is an important factor in hindering the growth of small and medium enterprises.
In addition, Dr. said that the second phase of the project will support small and medium enterprises to get easy and appropriate financing to increase economic diversification and to ease the burden of customers of banking and financial institutions during The time of the outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
On April 3, 2020, the Ministry of Economy and Finance launched a joint venture financing project to support small and medium enterprises worth $ 100 million.
