Personal administration is one of the three other types of government, including public administration, commercial governance, and social governance.
Individual governance is established by the Board of Trustees to transfer assets or funds to the Board of Trustees for management, management and maintenance for the benefit of the Board of Trustees themselves or for specific individuals (Law on Public Administration 2019). .
This person is defined in terms of rights, obligations and responsibilities with the agreement between the governor, the principal and the beneficiary through the letter of the governance.
The establishment of an individual administration may be made under the conditions that (1) the borrower is a natural person who donates his property or funds to the bureaucracy for his own benefit or the benefit of another person; or (2) the transfer of assets. Or funds by the surviving trustee and must make a letter of administration with the confirmation of the notary, the lawyer, the commune / sangkat, or the case of the trustee committing the inheritance at the time of the trustee.
