Duke Pung Kheav Se emphasized that this is a task that Nadia Bank contributes to the development of the national economy so that Cambodia has a good economy and the income of the people has increased and reached a high middle income country in 2050, but if we agree again, in 2040, Cambodia will achieve. General knowledge: What are the traditional Khmer architectural styles?
(Phnom Penh): Style refers to the architectural art form in the construction of temples, structures, decorations, carvings, sculptures, which architects, sculptors and artists strive to select at the will of the King. Ancient Khmer kings and nobles participated in the construction of many temples and architectural structures in different styles.
Among the ancient Khmer architectural arts, archaeologists have divided up to 13 distinct styles, including:
1: Phnom Da style
The construction of this style of architecture was at a time when the Chenla Empire was split in two in the 8th century. Temples classified in the Kampong Preah style include Kampong Preah, Ak Yum (ancient), Trapeang Phong (ancient). Almost all of the temples are built like in the past, on the plains, except for one temple, which is built on several floors.
The Kulen style was developed from the beginning of the 9th century to the end of the 9th century during the reign of Jayavarman II (802-850), with capitals in many places, such as Indrapura, Koti, Hariharalaya, Aramendrapura, Mahendrabat. The temples included in this style include the group of temples on Phnom Kulen, the Elephant Trom Temple, etc. 6: Preah Ko style
Angkor Wat style was established in the first half of the 12th century during the reign of King Suryavarman II (1113-1145), which also had the capital city of Angkor. Temples incorporated in this style include Angkor Wat, Beng Mealea, Banteay Samre, and more. In this style, Khmer architecture flourished to the top. The temples built in the style of Angkor Wat are dedicated to Vishnu or Narayan.
