(Banteay Meanchey): After the Royal Government of Cambodia reopened the border on August 13, a large number of Cambodian workers returned from Thailand. To ensure that Cambodian workers from Thailand do not transmit Kovid 19 virus, especially the virus that infects their families and communities, troops stationed along the border in Banteay Meanchey province are paying close attention to their health. Before sending them to the Chattalysak Center.
From the afternoon of August 14, 2021 to the morning of August 15, more than 900 Cambodian workers from Thailand entered Cambodia through O Bei Choan, in which 159 positive Kovid 19 were found. .
On the morning of August 15, 2021, Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division and Commander of the Security Command, organized the 5th Infantry Division to fight Kovid-19 disease. Take samples of Cambodian workers who have returned from Thailand at O Bei Choan before sending them to Chattalysak Center.
Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin pointed out that after the reopening of the border, some Cambodian workers returned to their hometowns through the three designated checkpoints in Banteay Meanchey province, and some cheated brokers and continued to sneak into restricted areas. However, they were arrested by the joint forces and sent for medical check-ups and follow-up measures.
During the inspection of the situation at O Bei Choan, General Seng Thearin also visited the front line forces of the 1st direction of Banteay Meanchey and ordered all forces to be very careful during the operation to prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19 and the new virus that Delta at the border line to implement "3 do not 3 protect" to ensure the safety of personal and teammates.
Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin thanked all the forces who worked tirelessly day and night to carry out the operation to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and the new Delta virus along the border. For the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people.
