What is happening in Afghanistan today is exactly the same as what happened in Cambodia and South Vietnam 45 years ago. Forty-five years ago, apart from being abandoned by the United States, the South Vietnamese regime collapsed and the South Vietnamese who had worked for the United States were in danger.
The words of Prince Sisowath Sirikmatak to the US Ambassador are historical lessons that Cambodian children should know:
I sincerely thank you for the message inviting me to your free country. But sadly I could not leave this country in such a cowardly situation. For your Excellency and especially for your great power, I have never believed in a single minute that His Excellency had the idea of abandoning a people to choose freedom.
His Excellency refused to provide them with protection and we can do nothing about it. Your Excellency has left us and I wish you and your country peace. But you must remember that I am willing to die here in the country I love, it is very bad because we have to be born and die one day inevitably. "My only mistake is to trust you, the American."
The stagnation of 45 years of history in Indochina is now re-emerging in Afghanistan.
Who are the victims on behalf of the Afghan people? Only the people of Afghanistan themselves! Both what happened in the Indochina War in 1975 and in Afghanistan now is another new argument about excessive foreign trust and over-indulgence, because in diplomatic relations there is no word for friend or foe. Only benefits, and if there are no more benefits, will be abandoned.
Siem Reap is one of the provinces most affected by Kovid 19 virus. As of August 12, the Siem Reap provincial administration had 19 cases of positive Kovid 19 and 5,956 cases. Of those, 3,714 were treated and 65 died. To date, Siem Reap still has a high rate of 19 cases of Kovid, despite the provincial administration's strict prevention measures.
During the outbreak of Kovid 19, individuals took great care to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to protect themselves from Kovid 19 or their families. Ms. Siv Lang also pays close attention to protecting herself from Kovid 19 when going out.
Ms. Hor Sivlang shared her experience in preventing Kovid 19. Every time she went out or went shopping, she always had to wear an alcohol mask. When you return home, take off your clothes and take a shower.
Ms. Siv Lang described it this way: "Normally, when I go out, I know that the bottle of alcohol is still there and I wash my hands often when I go out, when I touch something, I have to spray alcohol. When you return home, wash your hands thoroughly and spray alcohol. When I got home, I immediately took off my clothes and took a shower to communicate with the family.
In addition to the implementation of measures, Siem Reap has also been rushing to vaccinate people against Kovid 19 to help prevent Kovid 19 infection. About 500,000 people in the province have been vaccinated. Some of them have already injected both doses, some have already injected 1 dose and some are continuing to inject the second dose.
Hor Sivlang, like people in other provinces, has already been vaccinated against Kovid 19. She said the vaccine was important for health in the fight against Kovid 19 and called on people who have not yet been vaccinated to get it.
"I think people should come and get vaccinated as soon as possible," Sivang said. This vaccine can protect us from infection, and if the disease enters our body, it can help prevent us from getting serious without endangering our lives. "So this vaccine is really important for us."
The vaccination process in Siem Reap is covered by troops from the 4th Army Division. Ms. Siv Lang praised the vaccination team of the 4th Army Division for its good work and high attention to those who came to vaccinate.
Vaccination against Kovid 19 is a task that the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, pays the utmost attention to in the mission to fight Kovid 19 to protect the well-being of the people. So far, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 9 million people. This result has led to the assessment that Cambodia is doing well, fast and doing well compared to other ASEAN member countries.
The Siem Reap resident thanked Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen for seeking the vaccine, as well as setting out plans for the people to be vaccinated against Kovid 19. Ms. Siv Lang also thanked all stakeholders for their efforts to vaccinate to protect the lives of the people.
