Electronic payments increase, in the last 3 months, "Bakong" has more than 200,000 users
(Phnom Penh): During the outbreak of Kovid 19, the use of electronic payments has increased because people do not want to use banknotes directly, because the use of banknotes can cause transmission of Kovid 19 .
In fact, in the last three months, the number of electronic payments "Bakong" has increased significantly, with more than 200,000 downloads.
This was stated by Ms. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, during the official launch of the Maybank-Bakong cross-border money transfer service between Malaysia and Cambodia, organized by the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia and Maybank on August 12, 2021.
Ms. Chea Serey said, "Bakong electronic payment system is really important in the context of the spread of Kovid 19 while everyone is implementing the security gap as well as reducing direct money transfer transactions." "It's a good thing we set up an electronic payment system in Bakong before the outbreak of Kovid 19."
Ms. Chea Serey said that the Bakong electronic payment system provides a good option for customers to transfer money without having to worry about other parties using services other than their own banking services.
"We have seen a dramatic increase in mobile banking payments in recent years, from 2019 to the end of 2020," she added.
She added: "Speaking of the Bakong system, as of the end of March, the number of downloads of the Bakong program was only 100,000 downloads, which figure did not make me happy, even though the Bakong system did not create much. "By October 2020, I expect the number of uses to be higher."
"During April 2021, there was a long travel blockade, when we saw that the number of searches for the Bakong app on mobile phones increased in just three months, the number of Bakong users," she said. Doubled. As of the end of June, the number of people downloading the Bagong app has reached 200,000 downloads, and there are more than 2 million people who know the bagong so far.
Please be informed that people have switched from cash payment to electronic payment to help reduce the spread of Kovid 19 through the use of banknotes without proper cleaning. This change has led to a significant increase in electronic payments.
In the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has also encouraged banks and financial institutions and institutions in Cambodia to encourage customers and enterprises to opt for electronic payment transactions instead of banknotes.
In fact, many banks and enterprises have come to use electronic payments, including ACLEDA Bank Plc.
