In July 2021, the police cracked down on 329 drug crimes, arrested more than 800 suspects and confiscated a total of 219 kilograms of drugs
(Phnom Penh): In the period of July 1, 2021, the police cracked down on a total of 329 drug crimes, a decrease of 48 cases, compared to June, arrested a total of 849 suspects, an increase of 47 people 5.2 percent compared to June 2021 and seized a total of 219 kilograms and 460.71 grams. This is according to the official Facebook page of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, posted on August 13, 2021.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said: "Today, I would like to inform my compatriots again about the results of the operation to crack down on drug crimes in July 2021. In the first month, we cracked down on a total of 329 drug offenses, a decrease of 48 cases compared to June. Crimes include: 242 cases of trafficking, 84 cases of consumption, 1 case of synthesis and 2 cases of cultivation.
In connection with this case, a total of 849 suspects were arrested, an increase of 47 cases, equivalent to 5.2 percent compared to June 2021. The suspects were involved in 510 trafficking and storage cases, 331 drug use cases, 5 cases of synthesis and processing and 3 cases of cultivation. The suspects were 776 Cambodians and 73 foreigners.
In the crackdown on drug crimes in July 2021, the police seized a total of 219 kilograms and 460.71 grams of drugs. "Although the number of drug busts decreased from June, the number of drugs seized by the authorities increased to 73 kilograms, which is more than 50 percent compared to the previous month."
Remarkable! In 5 cases of drugs from 1 kg, equal to 5 groups, 13 suspects were arrested, including: 1 ringleader and 12 network members, including 8 Cambodians, 1 Chinese, 1 ethnic Four Vietnamese. In total, these five major cases contained a total of 213 kilograms of drugs, 834.08 grams, and 7 kilograms and 782.58 kilograms of chemical compounds.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized, "Dear compatriots! On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, on behalf of the Ministry of Interior and myself, I would like to extend my sincere appreciation and encouragement to all relevant leaders and officials, including civilians, police and the military police, who have worked well together. In the operation to crack down on drug crimes to contribute to the protection of security, public order and social security for the nation and the people.
Once again, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng would like to send a message to our compatriots from all walks of life and all law enforcement forces to support and implement the three national slogans and protect one report:
* Not involved: Do not trade, do not distribute, do not be a backbone, do not conspire and do not use drugs. Do not intervene: Do not prevent law enforcement from drug offenders, even family, relatives or friends. * Do not exempt: Do not relax law enforcement on drug offenders. All relevant authorities must enforce the law strictly and honestly in their profession, and everyone must respect and enforce the law.
One Report: Report to the authorities on the subject of trafficking, distribution, use, processing and illegal drug storage sites to the authorities… so that we can continue to join forces with the National Solidarity Against Drugs, which is the enemy of economic, social and resource development. People, especially youth resources, which are the pillars of the nation. Two new investment projects worth $ 5.5 million have been approved.
