(Phnom Penh): The army is the front line that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, gives priority to vaccinating the third dose (boost dose) to increase antibodies to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease. The decision to provide the third dose of vaccine to the army was a priority because the army has been actively fighting the Kovid 19 virus.
The army was a special force of the Royal Government during the fight against Kovid 19. They not only assisted in vaccinating the people, but also participated in other interventions, such as the implementation of measures to block food distribution, including the transportation of workers returning from Thailand.
The army is a core force that has always been indispensable on the battlefield of the 19th Kovid War and is also facing the Kovid 19 attack. Although they face the onslaught of Kovid 19 virus, they do not shy away from the tasks assigned to them by the government.
The decision to give priority to the army to get the third dose of vaccine by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, shows a high concern of Samdech Techo to the army. The decision also brought joy to the army.
Lt. Gen. Sok Rina, Deputy Chief of Staff and Chairman of the Kovid 19 Vaccination Team of the 4th Army Division, who is leading the vaccination campaign for the people in Siem Reap, sees the third dose as a help. Increase the body's immune system to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, especially the new mutation virus.
Lt. Gen. Sok Rina stated, "For this third dose, I personally feel like I have no reaction at all. My health is good and it may make us increase our immune system to be stronger. Resist the spread of Kovid 19 infection. "Especially the new type ."
Yean Raksmey, a military officer serving at the 4th Military Hospital and who is also involved in vaccinating the people, said that the third dose was very important for him to protect himself from the 19-virus Kovid attack. Can continue to stand up and help vaccinate people to move forward.
"This third dose to boost the first and second doses can be said to be a stronger vaccine because we have given three doses," said Yean Raksmey, 27. "After the third dose, we are confident that we can be more confident."
Regarding the symptoms after the third dose of AstraZenica vaccine, General Ith Sarath confirmed that his health was normal and there was nothing wrong. On the contrary, this third dose gives him high confidence in protecting his health from Kovid 19.
Cambodia has become one of the few countries in the world that has taken care of the health of its people, fought against Kovid 19 and achieved a rapid vaccination plan. This achievement would not have been possible without a clear plan and a clear plan from the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Cambodia's success in vaccinating the military has made Yean Raksmey military officer satisfied and regarded Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a great leader for him.
"We can say that Samdech Techo is a great leader because the countries around us have a lower percentage of vaccinations than our country," said Yean Raksmey. "In Cambodia, we can say that we are at the forefront of providing vaccines to our people until we reach the third dose."
With the opportunity to be vaccinated in the third dose, the troops not only expressed their happiness, but also expressed their deep gratitude and appreciation to Samdech Techo, who always paid high attention to their well-being.
Lt. Gen. Sok Rina expressed his gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, saying, "I would like to express my deep gratitude to the head of the Royal Government, who always thinks that he does not have time to rest day and night, burning his hands and feet to make sure that his children get the third dose of vaccine."
On the other hand, Yean Raksmey fighter expressed his gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen as follows: "Samdech Lok tried to burn his hands and feet to find a vaccine for the front line army to serve our people, because the Kovid 19 virus is very aggressive."
It should be noted that the vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense started the third dose on August 9, 2021. As of August 11, the third dose vaccination team had nearly 80,000 people.
According to General Ith Sarath, the Ministry of National Defense's vaccination team is responsible for vaccinating more than 300,000 troops, families, veterans and border police. General Ith Sarath confirmed that in the plan, the working group plans to give the third dose to people in this plan to be completed within 10 days.
