98.99 million rural poor in China lift out of poverty
BEIJING, Aug. 12 (Xinhua) - The State Council of the People's Republic of China (PRC) has released a white paper on "Achieving Social Welfare in All Perspectives: The Great Achievement of the Country's Human Rights Development." China.
According to the current poverty standard, the average annual per capita income of rural Chinese people is below 2,300 yuan, by the end of 2020, 98.99 million poor people will be living in poverty. China has been lifted out of poverty, 832 poor districts and 12.8 million poor villages have also been lifted out of poverty.
The White Paper points out that since the reforms, according to current poverty standards, 770 million rural poor in China have been lifted out of poverty. According to the World Bank's International Poverty Standards, the number of people who have reduced poverty is more than 70% of the world's population who have reduced poverty in the same period.
China has achieved the poverty reduction goal of the "United Nations Sustainable Development Agenda 2030" within 10 years, which has significantly contributed to the development of global poverty reduction and human development. Farmers in Chea Khlang commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province complain about the sharp fall in sugarcane prices due to Kovid 19 (Video inside)
