Cambodia-Malaysia launches cross-border money transfer service
This cross-border remittance service will allow Maybank customers in Malaysia to transfer money directly to family, friends or business partners in Cambodia via the MAE app, simply by using the registered recipient's phone number. Use Bakong software.
According to the National Bank of Cambodia, in the first phase, customers can transfer money from Malaysia to Cambodia, while the money transfer operation from Cambodia to Malaysia will be launched in the next phase.
Maybank customers can also enjoy a convenient, safe and affordable user experience. In addition, customers can transfer money up to 2,500 US dollars (equivalent to 10,000 ringgit) per day.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, congratulated the team of the National Bank of Cambodia and the Maybank team for achieving this excellent achievement.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "I am confident that cross-border payments and remittances between Cambodia and Malaysia through the Bakong system will help the two countries achieve a deeper level of financial cooperation in "Using technology to serve the people of both countries, especially Cambodian workers working in Malaysia, need to transfer money to support a safe and low-cost family life."
"In addition to promoting the development of financial technology and improving the connectivity of cross-border payment transactions between Cambodia and Malaysia, cross-border remittances to Cambodia that are easy, fast and low cost are also a way," she added. To accelerate the financial environment of the needy community as well.
He added that this is in line with Maybank Cambodia's goal of focusing on creating a digital network to provide customers with a smooth and worry-free banking experience. We are proud to support the move towards a cashless society in Cambodia and to accelerate the financial environment, especially in communities without access to financial services.
