This statement was made by Mr. Neth Pheaktra at a press conference on the hearing of the appeal in Case 002/02 against Khieu Samphan, former Chairman of the President of the Democratic Kampuchea regime on 12 August 2021 This.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, "Of that amount, 330 million US dollars from the voluntary contributions of the donor countries, of which 94.74 million US dollars was spent by the national side of the tribunal. The international side of the Khmer Rouge tribunal spent $ 235.35 million.
Three other former Khmer Rouge leaders were killed, including Nuon Chea, a former deputy secretary of the Communist Party of Kampuchea and chairman of the National Assembly, who died on August 4, 2019. Appeal in Case 002/02 in which he was sentenced by the Trial Chamber with Khieu Samphan to life imprisonment.
Case 002/01 against Nuon Chea and Khieu Samphan was finally closed by the Supreme Court Chamber, which sentenced him to life in prison.
The Trial Chamber of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) held a preliminary hearing in Case 002 against former Khmer Rouge leaders Nuon Chea, Khieu Samphan, Ieng Sary and Ieng Thirith in June 2011. Since then, at least Case 002 has been split into separate hearings, each hearing addressing different parts of the subpoena.
