(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has issued a decision to temporarily suspend private gatherings or gatherings of more than 15 people for an additional 14 days from zero on August 13, 2021. Until August 26, 2021. This is according to the decision that Fresh News received on the evening of August 11, 2021.
In this decision, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration also decided to waive the following cases:
* First: Meeting among family members living in the same house or shelter
* Second: Organizing funerals in accordance with the regulations of the competent authorities and after taking the body samples for analysis with Kovid-19 virus with negative results.
* Third: Meetings of public institutions, gatherings and meetings of health workers to implement health measures, such as taking samples to test for Kovid-19 and Kovid-19 vaccination.
* Fourth: Meeting of health workers who perform other emergency work
* Fifth: The meeting of the competent authorities and the forces of the Administrative Unity Command at all levels to maintain security, order and public order.
* Sixth: Gathering of people during the proceedings of a judicial police officer or a tribunal
* Seventh: The gathering of people who are necessary to serve the public interest or for other purposes as determined by the competent authorities.
