* Political geography and change of mindset of Chinese leaders
* Why is China paying attention to its nuclear arsenal?
During the Cold War, the former Soviet Union sought to maintain a large arsenal of nuclear weapons so that it could speak on an equal footing with the United States. Today, it may not be much different, as China is increasing its nuclear arsenal, believing that Washington will not give up its anti-China policy until China has the power to intimidate the United States.
* The future of the China-US arms race
At a recent public conference in China, a senior Chinese nuclear expert noted that when it comes to the current arms race between the United States and China, it is very similar to the run. The arms race between the United States and the former Soviet Union in the early 1960s was similar. Such a conclusion means that China and the United States are in the early stages of the nuclear arms race.
