Ministry warns to revoke the license of mobile phone companies that continue to sell and distribute SIM cards without user ID
The warning came after the ministry found out that Viettel (Cambodia) and Smart Asiata Co., Ltd. were selling and distributing SIM cards in a number of locations without the need for identification. Consumers.
This action demonstrates the continued implementation of the Inter-Ministerial Circular No. 001 dated 28 February 2012 and the directives of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia.
In order to strengthen the order in the telecommunications sector and national security by preventing the use of SIM cards without proper identification, the Ministry has confirmed that it will take action against both mobile service providers by requiring the immediate cessation of SIM sales and distribution. The card without taking the user's identification documents in any form or means from the date of this notice.
In case the fraudster buys the SIM card without the identification document from the company to commit the offense even though the company did not commit, it means that the company has contributed to the offense or conspired with the fraudster indirectly.
If the mobile service provider still does not follow the above steps, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will take the following actions:
1: Suspend or revoke the license to operate the mobile phone service 2: Freeze all requests of the operator 3: Take other measures in accordance with Article 78 of the Telecommunications Law 4: All persons involved in the above cases will face Criminal law.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will continue to monitor and take the strictest action in accordance with the laws and regulations applicable to any mobile service provider that has committed an illegal act.
