Takeo provincial authorities suspend excavation activities at 4 locations in Ta Mok Lake after finding violations of licenses
(Takeo): The excavation site of 4 out of 5 places around Ta Mok house in Roka Sangkat, Daun Keo City was led by Mr. Khan Sokha, Deputy Governor of Takeo Province this morning, August 11, 2021. Investigated and ordered to suspend activities for a while after finding some irregularities to the excavation.
Mr. Khan Sokha said that four companies had violated the licenses to apply for land reclamation rights to restore the lake, as they were larger and deeper than allowed by the department.
The Deputy Governor of Takeo Province said that after inspecting 5 pit sites and finding 4 breaches of breach of contract, he will make a report to the Governor of Takeo Province to check whether the licenses of 4 companies will be revoked. This comes after finding that the offense is serious or renewing the license just by educating them.
Mr. Khan Sokha added that through the actual inspection, the licenses of the four land reclamation companies should be revoked at once, because the land reclamation of those companies was not in accordance with the technical specifications, especially not respected. According to what it requested to the provincial authorities.
It should be noted that according to the leaked information from the officials who participated in the inspection, there was an official from Takeo Provincial Hall in charge of finance who was the one who took the land for all these companies. The official has been involved in scandals in the past to use the provincial hall's one-stop shop to buy land for sale, leading to a complaint to the Anti-Corruption Unit.
