The following is a complaint from a police officer: Residents in Plou Touk commune request the authorities and professional officers to prevent the illegal clearing of state-owned flooded forest land and ask the authorities to distribute land legally to them. Also grow crops
(Kampong Chhnang): Residents of Plou Touk commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, have requested the authorities and professional officials to help prevent the clearing and destruction of flooded state land in 3 areas in Plou Touk commune, which is still small. Shelter for fish spawning and asking for land for them to grow crops.
Authorities distributed 20 meters of residential land to them, 100 meters deep, per family. However, the authorities also advised them not to clear the land for further clearing, as the authorities said that more than 100 meters allocated by the authorities was state-owned flooded forest land, so the authorities did not allow the cutting. The clearing can extend more than 100 meters. Authorities have promised to allocate land to them for cultivation.
