The Ministry of Agriculture acknowledges that the price of agricultural fertilizers is higher than in previous years due to the difficulty of importing and not being able to produce on their own.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has claimed that there are nine reasons why the price of agricultural fertilizer is more expensive than in previous years, including the difficulty of importing due to the Kovid 19 crisis and the inability to produce fertilizer. It has just made the price of agricultural fertilizer in Cambodia more expensive.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, agricultural production in Cambodia in 2021 saw a significant increase in demand, while the demand for pesticides and fertilizers increased by 2020 with the import of pesticides. According to the import permit, there are 103,005 tons of pesticides and 1,406,775 tons of agricultural fertilizers.
At the same time, the price of agricultural fertilizers is also more expensive than last year, starting from the following main reasons:
1. In countries that produce pesticides and agricultural fertilizers, export can not produce in response to orders from Cambodia.
2. Raw materials are in short supply from major producers such as China, Malaysia and the United Arab Emirates.
3. Fertilizer production has been reduced due to the spread of Kovid-19, as in China, Thailand and Vietnam.
4: Transportation takes a long time due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease (health precautions and health regulations).
5: Along with orders from Cambodia in other countries also ordered, so the supply is not enough to meet demand.
6: The cost of rearranging the packaging that needs to be printed in Khmer.
7. Some fertilizers and pesticide suppliers do not go to the factory directly to the broker, which makes the fertilizer more expensive than the factory price.
8. The demand for domestic agricultural fertilizers has increased significantly as some investors have switched from other sectors to invest in agriculture.
9. Cambodia has not yet been able to produce agricultural fertilizers (only natural fertilizers and organic fertilizers can be produced). This coming August 16th
