According to the instructions, the General Department of Taxation would like to advise taxpayers under the self-declaration regime who engage in rubber plantation business in Cambodia to recognize income and expenses for the following income tax purposes:
1: Recognition of taxable income
Enterprises must recognize taxable income when supplying goods or services. The time of supply of goods or services is when the enterprise issues the invoice, if the invoice is issued before the delivery of goods or receipt of money, or when the delivery of goods or the completion of services or payment.
Revenues from the supply of those goods or services include:
A: Income from the supply of products: rubber, water or frozen rubber, crumb rubber B: Income from secondary business activities: Rubber seedlings, rubber trees, clearing services C: Other income, securities income, financial income
2: Expenses to be included in the cost of rubber trees
Enterprises must recognize expenditures according to the following principles:
2.1: All costs in the initial planting phase, from sowing to the beginning of harvest or sapling, which are directly related to the cultivation of rubber, are included in the early days of the rubber plantation. These costs include:
2.2: Expenses that are inconsistent with point 2.1 mentioned above shall be considered as operating expenses. Those costs include:
A: Expenditure on replacement for damaged crops: is any type of expenditure directly related to replanting, including other costs for plantation improvement, post installation of newly replaced crops after harvest. . On the other hand, in the case of a complete rubber plantation, the above 2.1 points shall be applied.
