Hun Many Calls on Young People to Protect Existing Achievements and Invest More for the Next Generation
The following is the full text of Hun Many's message to Cambodian youth:
"The fruit we are picking and eating is the result of more than four decades of hard work, planting and protecting trees, especially in the shadow of peace for the last 20 years.
* First: Know yourself well what we have gone through, especially the success of all the obstacles and challenges that as a whole society, we have gone through hardships by ourselves until today. We should be proud of our nation. Of course, in all circumstances we must remember that internal factors are the determinants and external factors are just the influences.
* Second: Bringing a country devastated by armed conflict to Cambodia today cannot be considered normal or ordinary. So what we proudly achieve is what we need to remember and turn into a force of will and spirit that Cambodians can do to continue their mission. Of course, we have achieved a lot, but much remains to be done for the better future of our nation and our people.
* Third: Learn to think together, think together, act together, take responsibility by considering:
At this point, as we all know, Cambodia has proudly achieved a development, but Cambodia is also in a position to continue to develop further by investing in strengthening our capacity as a nation in the field of defense. Foreign, national security, human resources, agriculture, industry, infrastructure, roads, competitiveness to provide an environment that attracts more foreign investment.
To create job opportunities for the people, especially the young people, which is a big basis for the national economy and to provide additional opportunities for the Royal Government to distribute all the benefits to the society, whether through public investment or the state. Politics, society, or in other words, state aid to the poor and vulnerable.
The above is something that, as young people, we can consider and find answers, both insights, mindsets and considerations of how and with what to achieve these goals, remembering that things can not It's not just imagining or just talking will work, because the future of the country and its people is so important that it can not be thought of simply and without thinking in detail, both in theory and strategy.
I also know that some people, both Cambodians and foreigners, come up with some ideas that are likely and simple, but should ask whether this idea is implemented in their country as a package, or just say that it has been implemented but there is no specific action. .
