"I am very pleased to be in this new position and I am even happier to be back in Cambodia 17 years from the time I ended my career in Cambodia as a team captain," said Maria Salim. Of related projects, social funds for community empowerment and poverty alleviation.
"I look forward to working with my Cambodian counterparts to help Cambodia manage the effects of the Kovid-19 epidemic, lay the groundwork for a vigorous economic recovery and resilience," she added. "To deal with the economic downturn in the future."
Previously in Cambodia, she was a Social Development and Human Resource Specialist, before moving on to senior positions in the World Bank's Operations Policy Division at its headquarters in Washington, DC.
