More than 200 villagers in Serey village, Khon Rang commune, Boribo district, protested for the removal of the chief abbot of Ang Serey pagoda, accusing him of misconduct and degrading Buddhism.
(Kampong Chhnang): More than 200 people who are Buddhists at the foot of Ang Serey pagoda in Serey village, Khon Rang commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, on the morning of August 8, 2021, gathered at Ang Serey pagoda to protest for the authorities. The pagoda's chaplain was expelled from the pagoda, accusing the monk of many wrongdoings and degrading Buddhism.
Meeting with journalists in Kampong Chhnang province, they expressed their dissatisfaction with the Chief Bishop of the pagoda, Bou Chanmony, who gave the following interviews:
* For the past 5 years, the Chief Inspector in the pagoda has not built anything, he has many things such as Pchum Ben, New Year, Kathin, Flower Festival after Buddhists came to celebrate in the pagoda, he took the suffix All left for personal use, nothing built.
* Local, provincial and national teams working to help the locals, who are philanthropists, helped build the Chan School. He did not support and did not agree to do so. Not only that, during the Krong Pali ceremony to raise the roof of Sala Chan, he came to stop them from doing it, but the people just overcame to get some roofing.
On the other hand, he treated people from far-flung provinces in the pagoda to stay in many pagodas in the past, regardless of the risk of Kovid infection. He took four of the children of the villagers to be ordained illegally. He has no morals, put the microphone, insult the government, play the microphone, listen to the song, the melody of Oun Bong, Indian chanting, magic, Om Am, put the microphone, brag about the monk's misconduct.
* He quarreled with the people in the pagoda and then complained to the district police, accusing him of trying to kill him. He does not accept invitations to home ceremonies, sometimes accepting them and not inviting them to wait until after the festival. 90% of the people are not happy with him, they have not entered the pagoda for 5 years.
Regarding the above allegations, he has the following denial:
It is true that the police officer came to pump water from the pagoda by truck, but he did not allow it to be pumped because he obeyed Samdech Techo's recommendation, because at that time there was a lack of water in the pagoda, the police did not go to pump wells elsewhere. Pump water from the well in the pagoda that is in short supply.
* His story The commune chief once promised the people that if he could not be expelled from the pagoda, the commune chief would be willing to return the commune seal to the district and province. The people raised him from the pagoda, he did not leave, even if he died, he did not leave.
The commune chief also asked him to leave the pagoda so that more than 1,000 people in the whole Serey village calmed down and came back to perform rituals in this pagoda again. Even the priests, if not resolved quickly, will have a bigger adhikari, because this dispute is very long, and if the fruit is ripe to fall.
Regarding the above case, Mr. Am Sophea, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, confirmed that the incident that happened in the above Ang Serey Pagoda is a long time ago and the province is trying to get the cult department to tell the provincial chief because he has appointed him as the acting chief inspector. This is not until the chief summoned him, however, the province is trying to solve this matter.
