Although she does not speak Khmer, Nay Vit confirmed through local authorities that after her vaccination, her health did not change, and that her diet and rest were normal. She also expressed her understanding of the value of the vaccine.
The grandmother, who lives in a remote area, said she was scared when she had not been vaccinated against Kovid 19, especially when she died and no villagers or family could celebrate. That's why he volunteered to get the vaccine.
She also thanked the Prime Minister for allowing him to be vaccinated and given him a gift on this occasion.
Please be informed that after the completion of the donation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Ms. O Vandin also continued to inspect the vaccination process for people in Ratanakkiri.
Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, emphasized that the vaccination campaign for the people in Ratanakkiri Province has so far achieved more than 60% of the plan, which is scheduled to be completed soon.
Two Unicity employees arrested after trying to lure people to borrow money from the bank to buy their products and escape
The commissioner confirmed that the arrest was made by people complaining about fraud.
The arrested UNICT employees are: 1. Name: Vith Sokren, Male, 27 years old, Occupation: UNICT staff, Residence: O'Kaki Village, Tang Krouch Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province. 2. Name: Chea Bin, Male, 41 years old, Occupation: Employee of Unicity Company, Residence: Kraing Pong Village, Khtum Kraing Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province.
According to the complaint, the two men recently claimed to have visited and sold Unicity's health supplements, claiming the quality and effectiveness of their treatment. Other.
In addition, they persuade and persuade customers to use the product, claiming to be profitable and have the opportunity to earn money from the company's product promotion, continue to change the status of ordinary users to Primary distributors, and some become area managers, also use cash to buy investment packages with companies.
After being persuaded, the two individuals, along with four other accomplices, introduced the plaintiffs to their $ 25,000 health supplement package, promising a monthly dividend of $ 3,000. USD will receive a gold card from the company for the work will go in the future, retire, receive a monthly stipend of 1,500 USD to 3,500 USD, and have the opportunity to travel abroad to travel to Europe and Asia. Etc.
After the explanation, the victim creditor agreed, but did not have the full amount. The person claiming to be a UNICT employee ordered the victim to take his personal property as collateral, instructing the private mortgage market to be quick and hassle-free, and assured that in the first month, the company would help pay the fees. Two months money.
After getting their money, they run away forever, nothing like the first promise, just promise this excuse that the company is managing to bring customers abroad and bring in new products. "Do not worry, the budget is not lost."
Major General Sam Samoun, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu, the two victims of the fraud were sent to court and the judge decided to detain them. Separately, four other factions of the provincial police force are also looking to arrest.
According to Major General Sam Samoun, in addition to the above cases, he also received other complaints as in the above case and is handling and searching for the victims.
The commissioner asked the people who lost their money through the above scam to file a complaint at the Kampong Speu Provincial Police so that he could take legal action to prevent such fraud from continuing.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Launches Third Vaccination for Frontline Officials in His Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province and Mr. Kheng Som, Chairman of the Provincial Council, on August 8, 2021, launched the third dose (boost dose) to frontline officials throughout the province at two locations: The main meeting of the provincial hall and at the provincial meeting hall of the Cambodian People's Party.
The front-line officials who received the third dose included the military, doctors and stakeholders who catered and treated Kovid.
The Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province said that the vaccine given to the front line officials at the third dose is a sacred provision from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who made every effort to find the vaccine and put it. Issue measures to inject to all our civil servants, so that the people must be grateful to Samdech.
(Phnom Penh): In implementing the measures throughout Cambodia on August 7, 2021, the competent authorities found another 1853 people and 1,048 vehicles violated a total of 1,165 cases of health and administrative measures and fined The fine is a total of 27.1 million riels. Of those who violated these measures, two were sent to court.
