Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia issues press release on the outcome of its Central Committee meeting
(Phnom Penh): This morning, August 7, 2021, the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia held its meeting to summarize its achievements and future direction, which was chaired by Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia. And the presence of a total of 200 members of the Central Committee and members of the meeting.
In the report summarizing the work results and further direction of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, it is shown that the work to strengthen and expand the organization of the CPPCC. Achieved its structure to the local level, with the municipal, district, Khan level reached 100% and the commune level reached 85.18%. There are about 180,000 members nationwide.
It should also be noted that within the framework of strengthening the organization of the CPPCC. The delegation of the Central Committee, led by Mr. Hun Many, met with members of the CPPCC. Structures across the country, having completed all 25 provincial capitals by the end of 2019.
Tomorrow, Kampong Thom Provincial Administration will reopen the entrance and exit of Spean Krong village in Stong district after being closed since July 30.
(Kampong Thom): The administration of Kampong Thom province on August 7, 2021 issued a decision to end the closure of Spean Krong village, Chamna Krom commune, Stong district from August 8 tomorrow after the closure. To control and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 since July 30.
