North Korea last week warned that military exercises between the United States and South Korea scheduled for August could undermine efforts to restore ties between the two Koreas. In response, the South Korean Defense Ministry said that Seoul and Washington were discussing plans for joint military exercises, but so far no decision had been made.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration announces that people who have not been vaccinated against Kovid before and those who have just reached 18 years old should go to Phnom Penh Referral Hospital for vaccination.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on August 7, 2021 issued a notice to people aged 18 and over who failed to receive the vaccine in the past vaccination campaign and Those who have just turned 18 years old should go to the Phnom Penh Referral Hospital for vaccination from tomorrow onwards.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration has confirmed that during the previous Kovid vaccination campaign, some people failed to get vaccinated, including pregnant women who have just given birth and those who have been subjected to cataracts. Treating the needy is essential. In addition, there are some young people under the age of 18.
Therefore, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration strives to provide this vaccine to the people at the Phnom Penh Referral Hospital, located at Lot 2, Street 134, corner of Street 169, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara. The above people can go to get the vaccine every 8:00 am to 5:00 pm from the date of this notice until there is a new notification.
